	('b006d77e-aec9-43d2-ab4b-33c74c61e376', '5157c388-9765-44fd-b828-6986622c5a4e', '2025-02-13 06:19:34.248528+00', '2025-02-14 20:32:51.806903+00', '{Educator,Mentor,"Curriculum Developer",Researcher}', 'Education is not just about imparting knowledge, but fostering a love for learning and developing critical thinking skills.', 'Designing and implementing innovative teaching methodologies', '{"Educational Technology","Student Engagement","Inclusion Practices"}', '{"Student-Centered Learning","Critical Thinking Skills","Inclusive Education"}', '', 'vtt_transcript', 0.85, false, 'stance_from_welcome', 'active', NULL, NULL, NULL, false, NULL),
	('aa5d3d23-ee10-4888-938d-ca0763cdeecf', 'ef31c6d4-75c1-405b-ae77-5a8d38b90562', '2025-02-13 06:24:12.053184+00', '2025-02-14 20:32:51.806903+00', '{"Curriculum Developer","Instructional Coach","STEM Facilitator"}', 'Believes in creating an interactive and student-centered learning environment that fosters critical thinking and innovation.', 'Designing project-based learning modules that integrate technology and real-world problem solving.', '{"advanced technology integration","effective assessment strategies"}', '{"project-based learning","student-centered approaches"}', '', 'vtt_transcript', 0.85, false, 'stance_from_welcome', 'active', NULL, NULL, NULL, false, NULL),
	('1b1f17b1-9b02-4b7d-ab06-77dea0552331', 'ea155ac4-eb3a-4e24-a4be-84f0143f4348', '2025-02-14 01:01:57.797683+00', '2025-02-14 20:32:51.806903+00', '{"Curriculum Developer","Educational Technology Specialist"}', 'Learner-centered with a balance of respect for standards, focusing on aligning natural interest and ability level with educational goals.', 'Teaching and integrating technology in the classroom', '{"Personalized Learning","Adaptive Technology"}', '{Mathematics,"Technology Integration"}', '[Test P.]: Hi, my name is Mike and I teach artificial intelligence mostly to teachers and leaders of teachers. I''ve taught precalculus section. I''m currently teaching  [Test P.]: precalculus at the moment.  [Test P.]: I''m teaching video production at the moment as well. Those are two courses I''m  [Test P.]: teaching at the high school level.  [Test P.]: And I hope to learn more about. [Test P.]: I hope to learn more about what students should learn now that we have tools to do some of our traditional thinking for us.  [Test P.]: So like. [Test P.]: Umm, if we ignore the concept of cheating. [Test P.]: In umm. [Test P.]: In the conversation about artificial intelligence, what becomes possible and what are the real repercussions of like skipping some steps? So like my son?  [Test P.]: Could learn how to type, but if you can just talk and that''s more natural than typing. Do I get to skip that step in his learning so that he can move on to  [Test P.]: other things? And the answer is probably yes.  [Test P.]: But yeah, I guess I wanna hear about people''s opinions. What to definitely not  [Test P.]: stuck with what to definitely not, umm, skip, etcetera.  [Test P.]: What else would I like to learn? [Test P.]: I think I''ll start with just that. [Test P.]: My stance when it comes to learning is. [Test P.]: I want to say it''s very learner centered and what I mean by that is I like to let the learner.  [Test P.]: Become curious and accelerate them towards wherever they''re curious about. [Test P.]: I am balanced by like having respect for the standards. Like those things were  [Test P.]: really thoughtful.  [Test P.]: So when we think about like my history as a math teacher, like, I don''t know everything there is to know about what every person needs to know about quantitative thinking, and people have done a really good job to write that down.  [Test P.]: Over generations and so. [Test P.]: So the teacher''s job. [Test P.]: Is to know the standards UMM and align them to natural interest and ability level.  [Test P.]: Which means starting with the line, so taking the learner from where they are to where they want to go. But.  [Test P.]: But also letting the standard play a role. [Test P.]: I''m tech forward, so I think that we should use the tools of our time. [Test P.]: Umm, and. [Test P.]: I work to help make that happen. So one of the parts of my stance is I''m ex.  [Test P.]: I''m accelerating.  [Test P.]: That piece through my work again, I teach at. [Test P.]: North Tahoe High School in. [Test P.]: Tahoe City, CA. I''m historically a math teacher. [Test P.]: And I have in the past been a curriculum and instruction coordinator, and I''ve also played various roles in technology companies.', 'vtt_transcript', 0.8, false, 'stance_from_welcome', 'active', NULL, NULL, NULL, false, NULL),
