,\"text\":\"Oh interesting, How else do you think about AI might help or support you in your role in your work that you''re doing now, even as a novice? You''re just \",\"startTime\":1739900222,\"endTime\":1739900229},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"starting in. \",\"startTime\":1739900229,\"endTime\":1739900233},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"Well, I think probably one of the hardest things and what I''ve been doing is finding language that both doesn''t underestimate the the capacity, the intellectual capacity of the person that having a conversation with. \",\"startTime\":1739900235,\"endTime\":1739900250},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"But also doesn''t make things more confusing than it has to be.\",\"startTime\":1739900251,\"endTime\":1739900255},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"And so the ability to clearly describe with no more complexity that is necessary without underestimating that that person is perfectly capable of understanding. \",\"startTime\":1739900257,\"endTime\":1739900268},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I think you''re going to find some great AI tools to help you with that. That''s \",\"startTime\":1739900271,\"endTime\":1739900274},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"a great way to describe that. \",\"startTime\":1739900274,\"endTime\":1739900278},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I''ve learned that as I use an AI tool like ChatGPT, I use that a lot.\",\"startTime\":1739900279,\"endTime\":1739900284},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"That it can be trained to get better at answering things and so it knows more. \",\"startTime\":1739900284,\"endTime\":1739900291},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"As I give it feedback like that phrase that you just said and described that so well, even if I were to talk to my GPT like that, it will help me to to be better at doing so and give feedback and remember that it''s like hiring a new intern to be my assistant. And they might be really smart, but I still need \",\"startTime\":1739900291,\"endTime\":1739900309},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"to train them to answer and to work like I want them to work. Yeah. \",\"startTime\":1739900309,\"endTime\":1739900314},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"Well, darn. Because sometimes they''re smarter than I am, and this I might be \",\"startTime\":1739900315,\"endTime\":1739900318},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"holding them back. Yeah. \",\"startTime\":1739900318,\"endTime\":1739900321},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Umm, yeah, yeah. Umm, on your screen. What does it say for yours? I''m guessing \",\"startTime\":1739900320,\"endTime\":1739900323},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"it''s not. Ask Lori. \",\"startTime\":1739900323,\"endTime\":1739900327},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"No, it says share how his AI changed your work as an educator.\",\"startTime\":1739900329,\"endTime\":1739900333},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"OK.\",\"startTime\":1739900332,\"endTime\":1739900332},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Great. And then there''s a more option on mine. I have a few bulleted items there \",\"startTime\":1739900334,\"endTime\":1739900339},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"that I could consider the tools or platforms you use, think about efficiency impact improvements and in in the case for for classroom teachers, reflect on changes in student engagement or you mentioned it with your daughter that engagement, how students are using AI tools. I like it. Anything else you want to add or \",\"startTime\":1739900339,\"endTime\":1739900357},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I''m ready for the next cartoon. \",\"startTime\":1739900357,\"endTime\":1739900361},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"And now I do have next.\",\"startTime\":1739900365,\"endTime\":1739900367},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Great. OK.\",\"startTime\":1739900368,\"endTime\":1739900369},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Oh mine said partner ready after you press next. So whoever presses next first \",\"startTime\":1739900372,\"endTime\":1739900377},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"gets the other partner to go. Oh, you already hinted at this. Take turns sharing \",\"startTime\":1739900377,\"endTime\":1739900381},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"with Lori. How do you think AI will change the role of learners in the future? \",\"startTime\":1739900381,\"endTime\":1739900386},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"OK, keep going with your thought. I''m curious, how do you think it''ll change? \",\"startTime\":1739900388,\"endTime\":1739900391},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"Well, I mean.\",\"startTime\":1739900394,\"endTime\":1739900394},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Roles of learners in the future.\",\"startTime\":1739900394,\"endTime\":1739900396},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"So I think that if if learners.\",\"startTime\":1739900398,\"endTime\":1739900403},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"Do not understand the benefit of actually doing the thinking themselves that it could be detrimental to learners if they use it as a tool to enhance their real learning. \",\"startTime\":1739900405,\"endTime\":1739900418},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"I think it''ll speed up the ability of people to.\",\"startTime\":1739900418,\"endTime\":1739900422},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"Collect information that they''re gathering on a subject and help it bring them new insights. But I am worried about. \",\"startTime\":1739900426,\"endTime\":1739900435},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"I think it''s something you said to me before that, you know, a brilliant idea that somebody had. I''m worried that the AI will get smarter, but we will get \",\"startTime\":1739900438,\"endTime\":1739900447},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"Dumber, you know, that we, we will give over. \",\"startTime\":1739900447,\"endTime\":1739900451},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"The task of actually thinking and learning the AI and become lazy.\",\"startTime\":1739900454,\"endTime\":1739900459},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Tell me more about what you mean by enhancing thinking for a human.\",\"startTime\":1739900460,\"endTime\":1739900464},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"So I I think that when I''m facilitating learning or when I''m taking responsibility for my own learning, I have to be actively. \",\"startTime\":1739900467,\"endTime\":1739900477},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"Engaged with the idea that I''m trying to expand my current understanding. Umm, \",\"startTime\":1739900478,\"endTime\":1739900483},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"I could be listening or reading or expressing myself just to confirm what I already know, or to convince somebody else to have the same thoughts. \",\"startTime\":1739900483,\"endTime\":1739900494},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"But when I''m really learning, I''m intentionally trying to find nuanced areas where I need to rethink or expand or get more clear. \",\"startTime\":1739900498,\"endTime\":1739900510},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"What do you see is maybe the role of AI tools to be that assistant or tutor to help do exactly what you were saying? \",\"startTime\":1739900512,\"endTime\":1739900520},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"I don''t know much about it, but if it could start to tell me when I''m resisting, you know, or. \",\"startTime\":1739900521,\"endTime\":1739900527},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"If it could tell me when I seem to be blocked.\",\"startTime\":1739900528,\"endTime\":1739900531},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"Or stuck in a rut. That would be nice. It would say, hey, Lori, you''re doing \",\"startTime\":1739900535,\"endTime\":1739900539},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"it again. You know, you''re so interested in systems that you''re. \",\"startTime\":1739900539,\"endTime\":1739900544},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"Not even thinking about other things or something like that, you know that you''re inappropriately. \",\"startTime\":1739900544,\"endTime\":1739900550},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"Going off on a systems thinking binge when this isn''t really directly related to that. \",\"startTime\":1739900550,\"endTime\":1739900554},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"That would be like a coach. I can see that like side by side with you being \",\"startTime\":1739900558,\"endTime\":1739900562},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"that coach and helping you clarify your thinking and giving that feedback. \",\"startTime\":1739900562,\"endTime\":1739900567},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"That''s great insight. I''m going to press more. I''m curious about it. Consider \",\"startTime\":1739900568,\"endTime\":1739900572},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"personalized learning experiences and then think about AI tutors or assistants. \",\"startTime\":1739900572,\"endTime\":1739900575},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I think we''re on that same page. \",\"startTime\":1739900575,\"endTime\":1739900578},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I really like how you were saying that about enhancing our thinking. And if \",\"startTime\":1739900579,\"endTime\":1739900583},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"it''s not enhancing our thinking and my, my thinking as soon as you said that Lori is like imagining a plant, the neurology of my of my brain. And if it''s \",\"startTime\":1739900583,\"endTime\":1739900592},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"not helping my neural pathways to grow deeper and stronger and more connected new pathways when I need them, if it''s not helping me grow them in a healthy way, then. \",\"startTime\":1739900592,\"endTime\":1739900606},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"It''s it''s replacing my thinking.\",\"startTime\":1739900607,\"endTime\":1739900608},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And then I''m like.\",\"startTime\":1739900609,\"endTime\":1739900610},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"It''s I don''t know, I just think of the click, click, click news feed or social media scroll, or I''m just doing something, but I''m not really growing helpfully in my mind. I''m just reacting with that dopamine hit and I''m just like clicking. \",\"startTime\":1739900613,\"endTime\":1739900628},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"But if it comes alongside to and your phrase was enhance my thinking, then I it for me, it gives me that visualization of really strengthening my thinking. \",\"startTime\":1739900628,\"endTime\":1739900638},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Like like as a as a weightlifter or bodybuilder or an athlete, I want to get stronger muscles, I want to get faster reaction times. I want to get better \",\"startTime\":1739900638,\"endTime\":1739900646},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"CS GO.\",\"startTime\":1739900645,\"endTime\":1739900645},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"at my thinking. And I really appreciate how you use that phrase enhance the \",\"startTime\":1739900646,\"endTime\":1739900649},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"thinking. \",\"startTime\":1739900649,\"endTime\":1739900653},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And if we''re using AI as a tool to enhance our thinking?\",\"startTime\":1739900654,\"endTime\":1739900657},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Even you said earlier about using the right words that are clear and concise but not so obscure that the the reader or the listener wouldn''t understand it, but also. \",\"startTime\":1739900658,\"endTime\":1739900670},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"That it''s not vague, but that could be a great feedback. I could use that as \",\"startTime\":1739900670,\"endTime\":1739900673},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"a tool to help me be better in my thinking, to be better in my writing, to be better in the way that I''m trying to describe something. And even as you called \",\"startTime\":1739900673,\"endTime\":1739900680},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"out that, hey, Jeff or Lori, you''re, you''re stuck or you''re way off target. \",\"startTime\":1739900680,\"endTime\":1739900684},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Get back to your goal. \",\"startTime\":1739900684,\"endTime\":1739900687},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Umm, yeah. I, I''ll share one quick thing that I, I loved about feedback. I had \",\"startTime\":1739900689,\"endTime\":1739900693},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"a bunch of words and I don''t remember what it was for, but I asked for feedback on a writing tool. And I was asking the AI assistant to give me feedback. And \",\"startTime\":1739900693,\"endTime\":1739900701},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"it said, hey, Jeff, these two paragraphs, you might consider joining to one because it looks like it''s one idea that you split apart. And I was like, oh, \",\"startTime\":1739900701,\"endTime\":1739900709},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"you''re right. When I reread it, that gave me the feedback to help enhance my \",\"startTime\":1739900709,\"endTime\":1739900714},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"thinking and clarify my writing. \",\"startTime\":1739900714,\"endTime\":1739900718},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Without replacing my writing or replacing my thinking, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1739900719,\"endTime\":1739900723},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"Uh-huh. Right, right. I can definitely see that. Uh, one of the other areas \",\"startTime\":1739900723,\"endTime\":1739900729},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"that feedback could be really helpful is in not sequencing. \",\"startTime\":1739900729,\"endTime\":1739900734},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"Concepts in the way that''s easiest for others to umm.\",\"startTime\":1739900734,\"endTime\":1739900738},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"Process so I think sometimes.\",\"startTime\":1739900739,\"endTime\":1739900742},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"Not I think I know people who give me feedback that I sometimes go in an unconventional sequence of what I''m talking about and that throws them. It doesn''t throw me. \",\"startTime\":1739900743,\"endTime\":1739900751},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"I''m totally comfortable with what I''m doing, you know, But I think I could get feedback on, you know, maybe not the most logical sequence here. Maybe you could \",\"startTime\":1739900751,\"endTime\":1739900759},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"reorder what you''re saying. \",\"startTime\":1739900759,\"endTime\":1739900764},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Oh, I like that. Yeah. It makes sense in our brains when we follow the paths \",\"startTime\":1739900765,\"endTime\":1739900769},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"that what''s their problem? Why don''t they understand and think like I think? \",\"startTime\":1739900769,\"endTime\":1739900774},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Oh, I like it. OK, I''m gonna click next.\",\"startTime\":1739900775,\"endTime\":1739900777},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"Mine says partner ready, that''s good.\",\"startTime\":1739900780,\"endTime\":1739900782},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Read the challenges under More and choose one. Take turns with Lori and look \",\"startTime\":1739900784,\"endTime\":1739900787},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"for common threads. \",\"startTime\":1739900787,\"endTime\":1739900790},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Oh, these are great. So either share a story. We''re all here for different reasons \",\"startTime\":1739900803,\"endTime\":1739900808},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"in your own word, what''s yours and solve a problem. What''s the problem of practice \",\"startTime\":1739900808,\"endTime\":1739900813},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"that Lori may be able to help you think or help you with think together and share wisdom experiences. Oh, OK, I''m gonna nose goes. You get to pick. \",\"startTime\":1739900813,\"endTime\":1739900822},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"OK, I''m going to because I am curious. I think you''re a good thinker and I''d \",\"startTime\":1739900824,\"endTime\":1739900826},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"like to go to challenge too. \",\"startTime\":1739900826,\"endTime\":1739900829},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"OK, what''s the problem or practice you''ve got?\",\"startTime\":1739900830,\"endTime\":1739900832},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"So I, I think the conflict in my mind is that when you''re trying to run an initiative \",\"startTime\":1739900833,\"endTime\":1739900839},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"in a school or in a district, there''s always people that would most likely be early adopters that, you know, come forward very anxious to do anything you''d ask to be on the cutting edge. And there are people who for lots of different \",\"startTime\":1739900839,\"endTime\":1739900856},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"reasons, some good and some self protective, hold back. \",\"startTime\":1739900856,\"endTime\":1739900861},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"But I''ve had a few experiences where the group that I was working with didn''t allow that to happen because they included everybody, let''s just say at the school level, even the cafeteria staff, the custodial staff, the secretarial staff, everybody was part of the initiative. And those were the most exciting \",\"startTime\":1739900864,\"endTime\":1739900882},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"initiatives I''ve been part of. \",\"startTime\":1739900882,\"endTime\":1739900886},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"And so the developing of stars or the taking on of early adopters and then thinking that they''re going to spread the idea to others has backfired when I''ve used it. It has caused the insurance and the outs. \",\"startTime\":1739900888,\"endTime\":1739900905},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"And yet I''ve worked.\",\"startTime\":1739900906,\"endTime\":1739900908},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"It seems as though in large schools there''s a lot of resistance to total.\",\"startTime\":1739900911,\"endTime\":1739900916},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"Involvement of everybody.\",\"startTime\":1739900917,\"endTime\":1739900919},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah, that''s a struggle. You don''t want to segregate your group to the haves \",\"startTime\":1739900922,\"endTime\":1739900927},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"and have nots, those who are welcomed and those who are by default or implied, not welcomed. And yet when you bring everybody together, it''s such a diverse \",\"startTime\":1739900927,\"endTime\":1739900936},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"group of individuals on not only their skill sets, but their willingness to change or adopt or to try something. \",\"startTime\":1739900936,\"endTime\":1739900946},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And that brings for all sorts of problems when it comes to the activities or the facilitation of learning or implementation of the initiative and all of those things. Yeah, I, I hear you there. \",\"startTime\":1739900946,\"endTime\":1739900957},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"And I think that, you know, I could characterize the two extremes that don''t become early adopters. \",\"startTime\":1739900958,\"endTime\":1739900966},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"There''s the ones who have failed often in the past so you know they''re not interested in. \",\"startTime\":1739900967,\"endTime\":1739900972},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"Welcoming another failure. And then there''s those that have been most successful \",\"startTime\":1739900973,\"endTime\":1739900977},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"in the current and they don''t want to lose their status. So it it seems like \",\"startTime\":1739900977,\"endTime\":1739900981},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"what you end up with, the most anxious people to move you forward are the people in the middle. But I find working with people at the extremes the most exciting, \",\"startTime\":1739900981,\"endTime\":1739900989},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"so I don''t want to leave them out. \",\"startTime\":1739900989,\"endTime\":1739900993},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Great insight. It sounds a lot like sorry but math classes in general. I want \",\"startTime\":1739900995,\"endTime\":1739901000},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"to work with the honors students is what I hear often. \",\"startTime\":1739901000,\"endTime\":1739901005},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Laurie, you''re really exciting. You''ve done your homework. Let''s keep you in \",\"startTime\":1739901007,\"endTime\":1739901011},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"our class. Jeff, you know I don''t want to work with you because you didn''t do \",\"startTime\":1739901011,\"endTime\":1739901015},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"anything and you don''t seem very interested in what we''re doing in class today. \",\"startTime\":1739901015,\"endTime\":1739901019},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Why don''t you go over to Mr. Mickelson''s classroom or somewhere else? And. \",\"startTime\":1739901019,\"endTime\":1739901024},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I think we''ve done a really good job of creating a horrible place in math land, in math classrooms over decades and decades of doing so. And it breaks my heart \",\"startTime\":1739901024,\"endTime\":1739901033},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"to see that. And it breaks my heart to see kids who, when I''ve been in a classroom \",\"startTime\":1739901033,\"endTime\":1739901037},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"when we were Co teaching with a group of kids, even though we named it Super cool Math Club because we wanted it to be the best for these individuals. They \",\"startTime\":1739901037,\"endTime\":1739901045},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"all knew why they were there. They looked around and just started laughing. \",\"startTime\":1739901045,\"endTime\":1739901050},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"We know why we''re here, Mr. Crawford. \",\"startTime\":1739901050,\"endTime\":1739901054},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Mr. Kozol, we know why we''re here and they knew it because they had failed for \",\"startTime\":1739901055,\"endTime\":1739901059},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"semester math in high school their freshman year. They had been failing math \",\"startTime\":1739901059,\"endTime\":1739901063},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"forever. They know what behaviors they had. They had been in trouble with all \",\"startTime\":1739901063,\"endTime\":1739901066},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"of these different things. We would segregate them because they just weren''t \",\"startTime\":1739901066,\"endTime\":1739901070},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"ready and the other teachers didn''t want to work with them. So I think what \",\"startTime\":1739901070,\"endTime\":1739901074},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"you''re talking about, it''s. \",\"startTime\":1739901074,\"endTime\":1739901078},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I don''t know what the right word would be. Speaking of assistance, please give \",\"startTime\":1739901079,\"endTime\":1739901083},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Jeff the right word. Endemic pandemic. But it''s everywhere and in everything \",\"startTime\":1739901083,\"endTime\":1739901087},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"in our system that we we tend to segregate for those who we believe already that we as teachers or leaders want to work with. And then the rest, we don''t \",\"startTime\":1739901087,\"endTime\":1739901094},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"work with them. It is exciting to work with early adopters. It is exciting to \",\"startTime\":1739901094,\"endTime\":1739901098},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"work with kids who are. \",\"startTime\":1739901098,\"endTime\":1739901102},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Interested and willing to learn and are ready and did their homework and have all their colored pencils ready and their notebooks clean. It''s easy to work \",\"startTime\":1739901103,\"endTime\":1739901109},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"with them. But I think that what you''ve you''ve described really well is that \",\"startTime\":1739901109,\"endTime\":1739901113},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"doesn''t work for the whole of the system. It works for that individual, for \",\"startTime\":1739901113,\"endTime\":1739901116},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"that teacher and for that kid, but it doesn''t work for the school and doesn''t move them forward. \",\"startTime\":1739901116,\"endTime\":1739901123},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"And as a matter of fact it it often moves them backward.\",\"startTime\":1739901124,\"endTime\":1739901128},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"Because the old system that everybody was used to, everybody was doing it moderately well. But now you''ve got strong resistors that that are gonna really confuse \",\"startTime\":1739901130,\"endTime\":1739901139},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"kids. I''m gonna do a little bird walk because of our connection in math when \",\"startTime\":1739901139,\"endTime\":1739901143},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"I retired for the first time long ago. \",\"startTime\":1739901143,\"endTime\":1739901148},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"I did volunteer work at the local elementary school and I started a math haters club and there were two requirements for the math haters club. The kids had \",\"startTime\":1739901148,\"endTime\":1739901156},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"to know they were smart and they had to hate math. And so from a teacher perspective, \",\"startTime\":1739901156,\"endTime\":1739901160},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"it was kids that were plenty smart, but they were really underperforming in math and. \",\"startTime\":1739901160,\"endTime\":1739901168},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"So those were the kids that I pulled out and worked with.\",\"startTime\":1739901171,\"endTime\":1739901174},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"And I worked with their parents and sent packets home with the parents with information about, you know, my insights into the thinking of their child and what might be holding them back in math. \",\"startTime\":1739901174,\"endTime\":1739901186},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"Well, there''s this one little girl that sticks out of my mind. So she was obviously \",\"startTime\":1739901186,\"endTime\":1739901189},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"smart. She had. \",\"startTime\":1739901189,\"endTime\":1739901191},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"Borrowing for the first time and it seemed to close her down in math, you know, she just couldn''t get it and was frustrated, didn''t want to do any math in class anymore. So I sat on the floor. I said, you know, I don''t know if you''re a self \",\"startTime\":1739901192,\"endTime\":1739901204},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"talker, you know, but if you could just talk while you''re doing the problem so I can see what your mind is doing. \",\"startTime\":1739901204,\"endTime\":1739901212},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"So she said, OK, look.\",\"startTime\":1739901214,\"endTime\":1739901215},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"That so she had a problem wearing the ones.\",\"startTime\":1739901217,\"endTime\":1739901221},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"Position the number was smaller than the one at the bottom and she says I know my teacher told me if the bottom number is bigger than the top number I have to borrow one from the 10s. So she says. But I have a few problems with that. \",\"startTime\":1739901221,\"endTime\":1739901234},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"First of all, I don''t know what to do with the other nine from the 10K. \",\"startTime\":1739901234,\"endTime\":1739901238},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"And the other thing is borrowing 1 is not going to be enough because when I borrow one from the towns I still won''t have enough to do the subtraction. \",\"startTime\":1739901240,\"endTime\":1739901248},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"And besides that my mom taught me if you borrow something you have to pay it back at some point and they haven''t told me how I ever pay back the one that I borrowed from the 10 from the 10s place. \",\"startTime\":1739901249,\"endTime\":1739901260},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"Now, so that''s a very creative mind, a complex mind who is? I mean, actually \",\"startTime\":1739901261,\"endTime\":1739901266},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"that was fascinating. I couldn''t have made that story up if I had wanted to. \",\"startTime\":1739901266,\"endTime\":1739901272},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Oh, that''s a wonderful story of where an individual is trying to assimilate all of the knowledge that they''re learning. Even the word borrow. Do you not \",\"startTime\":1739901273,\"endTime\":1739901282},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"borrowing anything? You''re you''re decomposing or unbundling A10 and you''re taking \",\"startTime\":1739901282,\"endTime\":1739901287},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"You''re never going to go like that.\",\"startTime\":1739901285,\"endTime\":1739901287},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"a 10s unit and you''re breaking it apart into usable ones, units. She didn''t \",\"startTime\":1739901287,\"endTime\":1739901292},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"have place value understanding, but you didn''t. \",\"startTime\":1739901292,\"endTime\":1739901297},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Know that until she started expressing her thinking and sharing her thinking and Laurie, I love how what you did is I always have in my mind the list of effective mathematics teaching practices and besides opposing purposeful questions, which is what you did. \",\"startTime\":1739901298,\"endTime\":1739901313},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"There is that the, the one that''s listed #8 as I think it says illicit and use evidence of student thinking. You elicited her thinking and then you could use \",\"startTime\":1739901314,\"endTime\":1739901321},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"evidence of her student thinking. But what a wonderful mind and what a great \",\"startTime\":1739901321,\"endTime\":1739901325},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"job of getting her to talk about it. \",\"startTime\":1739901325,\"endTime\":1739901328},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"It''s a, it''s a lovely bird walk. And what I think, what I have seen in my experiences \",\"startTime\":1739901329,\"endTime\":1739901334},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"with educators and with students alike, it doesn''t matter where we are on that spectrum of early adopters, how smart we are, how hateful of math we feel or \",\"startTime\":1739901334,\"endTime\":1739901342},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"wherever we are in the system and, and all sorts of things that you talked about, even with our own identity and wanting to protect our identity, I don''t want to look like this. I have a status now and I don''t want to, I don''t want anyone \",\"startTime\":1739901342,\"endTime\":1739901354},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"to attack that. \",\"startTime\":1739901354,\"endTime\":1739901359},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"All of those things in in the messy soup of learning for us as, as people, What I found is getting them to talk like you mentioned and having rich discourse is the best way when we start talking about what''s going on, when we start talking about, OK, we''re trying to subtract these numbers, but what''s really going on? \",\"startTime\":1739901359,\"endTime\":1739901380},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Then we can have rich conversations and then we can all move forward in our in our thinking. And then when we have rich discourse amongst a group, especially \",\"startTime\":1739901380,\"endTime\":1739901388},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"as adults, then we can share out those things when we''re ready to. And I can \",\"startTime\":1739901388,\"endTime\":1739901392},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"see the early adopters who are sharing out these things and I can watch and I can learn more from that. And I can also give from my stance wherever I am, \",\"startTime\":1739901392,\"endTime\":1739901401},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"if I''m in the middle or if I''m at the late adopters, I can share out my concerns or my worries or my observations of you. \",\"startTime\":1739901401,\"endTime\":1739901409},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And for me, I have to put it in a context of something like yesterday Anna and I were up at 49° N. \",\"startTime\":1739901410,\"endTime\":1739901417},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"It''s a snow park. Everyone''s welcome. I''m seeing little kids rolling on the \",\"startTime\":1739901417,\"endTime\":1739901421},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"snow. That was their their point of entry. That was their access. I see other \",\"startTime\":1739901421,\"endTime\":1739901426},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"people on weird old skis that aren''t that great, that they bought for super cheap because they got them and they want to go play in them. I see people on \",\"startTime\":1739901426,\"endTime\":1739901435},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"snowboards, people on skis, people dressing the way they want to, going where they want to, and having conversations with each other when they want to. \",\"startTime\":1739901435,\"endTime\":1739901443},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And in that place, that snow park, if we create similar learning circumstances in the math classroom and in the initiative space as you were mentioning, if \",\"startTime\":1739901444,\"endTime\":1739901454},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"we have that where everybody can access it and everybody can express themselves with their identity and their agency the way they want to, but they''re invited to play and they''re given some things like. \",\"startTime\":1739901454,\"endTime\":1739901468},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Lifts start at 9 and the lifts close at 3. Here''s the lifts, here''s the map. \",\"startTime\":1739901468,\"endTime\":1739901473},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"What are you going to do today? And if we can come alongside and help cultivate \",\"startTime\":1739901473,\"endTime\":1739901478},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"or enhance their thinking and enhance their learning for where they''re wanting to go, even bringing them together. This is a shared initiative that your school \",\"startTime\":1739901478,\"endTime\":1739901487},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"has. You''re the ski team. We want to help all of us to do XYZ. These are your \",\"startTime\":1739901487,\"endTime\":1739901492},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"goals that you have now. How do we come along and support you? \",\"startTime\":1739901492,\"endTime\":1739901496},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I think in in my lessons learned with the research that I''ve read and then practicality. \",\"startTime\":1739901497,\"endTime\":1739901502},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"In the classroom for little ones, all the way up through adult learners like yourself and myself. \",\"startTime\":1739901502,\"endTime\":1739901508},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"If we don''t have that.\",\"startTime\":1739901509,\"endTime\":1739901510},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"That task or that space like the snow park, where everybody can access and everybody has their own identity and agency. \",\"startTime\":1739901511,\"endTime\":1739901519},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"If we can''t put them at the controls a little bit and show them that they''re capable, we can''t do that, then it''s going to fail. \",\"startTime\":1739901519,\"endTime\":1739901526},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And segregating us, that''s even worse.\",\"startTime\":1739901527,\"endTime\":1739901529},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Granted, I think we do need to ask for some people at times. Here''s a cool new \",\"startTime\":1739901529,\"endTime\":1739901533},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"snowboard. You want to try it out. Who wants to try this out? And some will \",\"startTime\":1739901533,\"endTime\":1739901537},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"want to try it out and some won''t want to try it out. But it has to be done \",\"startTime\":1739901537,\"endTime\":1739901540},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"in the group still and not isolating people and telling them, Laurie, you have value, but Jeff, you don''t because you wanted to try the snowboard or this new AI tool, but Jeff, you didn''t, so you don''t have value. But we can''t do that \",\"startTime\":1739901540,\"endTime\":1739901552},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"anymore. It really shatters the whole of the community and it shatters the individual \",\"startTime\":1739901552,\"endTime\":1739901555},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"too, and who they. \",\"startTime\":1739901555,\"endTime\":1739901559},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"They are and they''re and they''re, they''re placed in that, in that community. \",\"startTime\":1739901560,\"endTime\":1739901563},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Now my brain wants to walk in all sorts of other places. \",\"startTime\":1739901563,\"endTime\":1739901567},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"What''s the?\",\"startTime\":1739901567,\"endTime\":1739901568},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"Yeah, now it''s interesting that you brought it into the world of skiing because. \",\"startTime\":1739901568,\"endTime\":1739901573},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"One of my major insights and sources of empathy is from the experience that the school I I mentioned I worked at. \",\"startTime\":1739901575,\"endTime\":1739901583},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"A school for gifted kids in the Valley, Pioneer School. And because Betty, the \",\"startTime\":1739901585,\"endTime\":1739901589},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"director of that, was also a ski instructor at Schweitzer, you know, on Friday during ski season, we took all the kids skiing. But the kids went skiing, you \",\"startTime\":1739901589,\"endTime\":1739901597},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"know, with ski instructors and the teachers and parents that could join us when skiing on our own. \",\"startTime\":1739901597,\"endTime\":1739901605},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"It happens that I''d like to blame it on the I grew up in Miami, you know, there was no snow there. I''d like to blame it on that. I was born premature, so I''ve \",\"startTime\":1739901607,\"endTime\":1739901616},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"got some neurological disorder or something. But bottom line, I was a horrible \",\"startTime\":1739901616,\"endTime\":1739901621},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"skier. And over the years that I was there, I kept proving to myself that I \",\"startTime\":1739901621,\"endTime\":1739901626},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"was a horrible skier and other parents and teachers that were very nice. \",\"startTime\":1739901626,\"endTime\":1739901630},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"Didn''t want to always leave me behind as we were skiing together down the hill, you know, so they would. \",\"startTime\":1739901631,\"endTime\":1739901636},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"You know, have their fun ski. And then they''d stop and wait for me, and then \",\"startTime\":1739901636,\"endTime\":1739901640},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"I''d get to where they were. And they were arrested because they''ve been waiting \",\"startTime\":1739901640,\"endTime\":1739901644},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"for me and a little bit bored. And I had just barely, you know, made it alive \",\"startTime\":1739901644,\"endTime\":1739901649},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"to where they were. And so they would take off again, right? And then there \",\"startTime\":1739901649,\"endTime\":1739901653},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"I was again, you know? \",\"startTime\":1739901653,\"endTime\":1739901657},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"Well, I realized that for many students.\",\"startTime\":1739901658,\"endTime\":1739901661},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"That''s what school is like. They''re working like crazy to try to keep up and \",\"startTime\":1739901662,\"endTime\":1739901665},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"when they think they get there, the group has taken off and left them in their powder again. \",\"startTime\":1739901665,\"endTime\":1739901672},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"And how different I would feel about myself if skiing was considered valuable instead of reading, writing and arithmetic in my society. How different my life \",\"startTime\":1739901672,\"endTime\":1739901680},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"would be. \",\"startTime\":1739901680,\"endTime\":1739901684},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"That was a big deal for me because it''s the only thing that I was sort of forced \",\"startTime\":1739901687,\"endTime\":1739901691},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"to do for 10 years and be bad at it for the whole 10 years, you know, and, and yet I, I, I could have enjoyed it actually, if I hadn''t been trying to keep up with people who learned it better and faster than me. \",\"startTime\":1739901691,\"endTime\":1739901705},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Oh, Lori, that''s a wonderful and a sad story. Thank you for sharing that. That''s, \",\"startTime\":1739901708,\"endTime\":1739901711},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"uh, that''s a lot of emotion, a lot of pain in there. \",\"startTime\":1739901711,\"endTime\":1739901715},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I''m sorry that your crew made you feel that way. I''m glad that they stopped, \",\"startTime\":1739901716,\"endTime\":1739901720},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"at least for you once in a while, and that they they hopefully. \",\"startTime\":1739901720,\"endTime\":1739901724},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"I mean, they were trying, they were trying to be good friends and colleagues, right? And, but I think that''s what we do in school too. We think we''re trying \",\"startTime\":1739901724,\"endTime\":1739901731},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"to be good facilitators of learning, but that''s what we''re doing to some of the kids over and over and over again. \",\"startTime\":1739901731,\"endTime\":1739901739},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah, alright. I don''t think we''ve solved the problem with practice, but I think \",\"startTime\":1739901737,\"endTime\":1739901741},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"that my mind is is abuzz with it. And I encourage you to challenge you to think \",\"startTime\":1739901741,\"endTime\":1739901746},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"about that snow park metaphor. And how do we take that? It''s a space where everybody, \",\"startTime\":1739901746,\"endTime\":1739901750},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"even if they were born in Miami and didn''t really want to ski, but they were welcome and there was place for you and there were access points for you all day long. And how do we navigate that is the big question. And I think it''s \",\"startTime\":1739901750,\"endTime\":1739901762},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"definitely. \",\"startTime\":1739901762,\"endTime\":1739901767},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Effective teaching practices and good materials and well thought out tasks and initiatives and the road ahead for for where they would go the ski paths if you would. \",\"startTime\":1739901768,\"endTime\":1739901779},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"The Trails.\",\"startTime\":1739901780,\"endTime\":1739901781},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"All right. Anything else on it that your mind is thinking about before we do \",\"startTime\":1739901783,\"endTime\":1739901786},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"Uh-huh. Yep.\",\"startTime\":1739901784,\"endTime\":1739901785},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"the next and last card? \",\"startTime\":1739901786,\"endTime\":1739901789},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"No, I think I''m ready to move on.\",\"startTime\":1739901790,\"endTime\":1739901792},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"OK, next.\",\"startTime\":1739901792,\"endTime\":1739901793},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Thank you, Lori. I learned that you grew up in Miami. That''s amazing. And that \",\"startTime\":1739901795,\"endTime\":1739901798},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"you''re, you''re, you''re still here in the Pacific Northwest, up in Kettle Falls. \",\"startTime\":1739901798,\"endTime\":1739901802},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I can''t think of anywhere that''s so different than Miami than up in the Kettle Falls area. \",\"startTime\":1739901802,\"endTime\":1739901808},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"Uh, well, mine''s a little more specific to your style. Umm, I continue to learn \",\"startTime\":1739901812,\"endTime\":1739901817},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"from you that careful listening is really important and maybe it goes back to that original detail you always. \",\"startTime\":1739901817,\"endTime\":1739901825},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"Listen carefully and repeat very specific phrases or very specific information. \",\"startTime\":1739901825,\"endTime\":1739901828},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"And that does allow me to know that you''re listening carefully, and I think I need to develop that habit as well. \",\"startTime\":1739901828,\"endTime\":1739901836},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Thank you, Lori. Appreciate that. I''m trying. It''s something that I''ve been \",\"startTime\":1739901838,\"endTime\":1739901842},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"working and growing in a lot because the way I was raised, you just tell them what it is. And if you''ve told them one time, they should know it and they should \",\"startTime\":1739901842,\"endTime\":1739901848},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"know how to do it. \",\"startTime\":1739901848,\"endTime\":1739901851},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And I needed to listen a lot better, so I''ve been working on that. So I appreciate \",\"startTime\":1739901852,\"endTime\":1739901857},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"the feedback. Thank you. All right, have a great day. I''m going to press end \",\"startTime\":1739901857,\"endTime\":1739901861},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"OK.\",\"startTime\":1739901859,\"endTime\":1739901859},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"and you can connect with other people. We''ll get you connected as best we can. \",\"startTime\":1739901861,\"endTime\":1739901865},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And the, The thing is, if you wanted to, you could just even click Start learning the the thing will spin for a while. If nobody''s online to connect to it, you''ll \",\"startTime\":1739901865,\"endTime\":1739901874},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"get a personal reflection. If you wanted to do that, you can or we''ll connect \",\"startTime\":1739901874,\"endTime\":1739901878},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"you and try to get you connected. \",\"startTime\":1739901878,\"endTime\":1739901882},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"With other people as well, so you can have these rich conversations with so many others. \",\"startTime\":1739901883,\"endTime\":1739901888},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"Uh-huh. OK. This is very exciting. I have one piece of feedback. It is very \",\"startTime\":1739901888,\"endTime\":1739901892},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"disturbing to me that most of your faces covered up. Is that gonna happen always \",\"startTime\":1739901892,\"endTime\":1739901897},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"on the phone or like, I mean, your eyes are very expressive, so it could be worse, right? But. \",\"startTime\":1739901897,\"endTime\":1739901906},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"It could be worth.\",\"startTime\":1739901905,\"endTime\":1739901906},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"But are you seeing? Yeah, Are you seeing just my eyes?\",\"startTime\":1739901906,\"endTime\":1739901910},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"It''s good feedback.\",\"startTime\":1739901907,\"endTime\":1739901908},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"No, I see your face and I see down below, I see the cards and I see my little window up in the corner. So I can see like from from your shirt, like the perfect \",\"startTime\":1739901912,\"endTime\":1739901922},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"portrait even above your head a little bit. So I''m wondering why on your phone \",\"startTime\":1739901922,\"endTime\":1739901927},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"it''s not coming through if it''s zoomed in or zoomed out or should hold it back a little farther. \",\"startTime\":1739901927,\"endTime\":1739901936},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"Well, it I mean there I''m seeing your whole face, but I''m just wondering if it''s something I''m doing on my phone setting that. \",\"startTime\":1739901937,\"endTime\":1739901945},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Get feedback.\",\"startTime\":1739901939,\"endTime\":1739901940},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"It might be like the Zoom as I do as well. I said in my phone settings the Zoom \",\"startTime\":1739901947,\"endTime\":1739901951},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"so the the fonts are bigger. I wonder if that''s part of it and it just makes \",\"startTime\":1739901951,\"endTime\":1739901955},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"everything bigger and then covers up more on the phone. Yeah. \",\"startTime\":1739901955,\"endTime\":1739901960},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"OK.\",\"startTime\":1739901956,\"endTime\":1739901957},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"I''ll check that. I''ll check that out. Thank you.\",\"startTime\":1739901960,\"endTime\":1739901963},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Hey, we''ll figure. We''ll figure it out in great feedback.\",\"startTime\":1739901962,\"endTime\":1739901965},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Thank you. Have a great day, Lori.\",\"startTime\":1739901966,\"endTime\":1739901968},{\"speaker\":\"11886\",\"text\":\"OK.\",\"startTime\":1739901967,\"endTime\":1739901967}]"', '2025-04-30 20:57:09.464619+00', '2025-04-30 20:57:09.464619+00', '{"type": "PAIR", "duration": 2081, "created_at": "2025-04-30T20:57:09.433Z", "session_title": "#ai_learning_tools", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "190", "name": "#ai_learning_tools", "tags": [{"name": "Dream Camp"}, {"name": "AI in Education"}, {"name": "Freemium"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('c17a3228-9cde-4ff3-880c-9f1045bdc1d1', 'f75f7f16-84b9-41ce-b842-2a77a9dd70b8', '138139', '"[{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"So 2 books umm.\",\"startTime\":1744724227,\"endTime\":1744724228},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"One, I''m in the middle of reading, actually. Yeah, 22, I''m reading right now. \",\"startTime\":1744724228,\"endTime\":1744724232},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"Well, I just read Zero to 1 by Peter Thiel. \",\"startTime\":1744724232,\"endTime\":1744724236},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"That was a really interesting book. And while it''s not like exclusively about \",\"startTime\":1744724237,\"endTime\":1744724241},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"technology, it kind of talks about sort of the, umm, sort of the, the, the, I guess like impetus and Dr. of like successful founders and like what makes \",\"startTime\":1744724241,\"endTime\":1744724249},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"them successful, particularly in a technology context. \",\"startTime\":1744724249,\"endTime\":1744724253},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"Also reading Ezra clients abundance. So I''m in the middle of that. I think that''s \",\"startTime\":1744724254,\"endTime\":1744724259},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"it''s a really interesting read thus far and puts a very different perspective sort of on the notion of scarcity and how we should be kind of rethinking. \",\"startTime\":1744724259,\"endTime\":1744724268},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"How we should be rethinking our approach to, well, just about everything.\",\"startTime\":1744724269,\"endTime\":1744724274},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"Uh, massively changed the way I approach.\",\"startTime\":1744724296,\"endTime\":1744724299},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"Teaching and learning. So I think you know from a personal level, my workflows \",\"startTime\":1744724299,\"endTime\":1744724302},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"have have changed dramatically. Where AI is, is oftentimes a starting point \",\"startTime\":1744724302,\"endTime\":1744724305},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"of a workflow. \",\"startTime\":1744724305,\"endTime\":1744724309},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"When it comes to anything that''s like strategic.\",\"startTime\":1744724309,\"endTime\":1744724312},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"Sort of process oriented.\",\"startTime\":1744724313,\"endTime\":1744724315},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"Data analysis synthesis, uh.\",\"startTime\":1744724315,\"endTime\":1744724318},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"Like producing material, the content generation, all those things have.\",\"startTime\":1744724319,\"endTime\":1744724325},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"Change dramatically and AI is part of my workflow there. Umm also then from \",\"startTime\":1744724325,\"endTime\":1744724329},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"the perspective as like a technology leader, I have to be thinking about how this can impact, umm, education both in the short term. Umm so how do we use \",\"startTime\":1744724329,\"endTime\":1744724337},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"AI to sort of manage the present, both teaching with it and teaching about it? \",\"startTime\":1744724337,\"endTime\":1744724341},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"But then also, how do we re envision what we do with it?\",\"startTime\":1744724342,\"endTime\":1744724345},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"Umm.\",\"startTime\":1744724367,\"endTime\":1744724367},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"Yeah, this is a great question. I think we need to be thinking about we have \",\"startTime\":1744724368,\"endTime\":1744724372},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"to assume AI will reach some level of AGI. \",\"startTime\":1744724372,\"endTime\":1744724377},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"Uh, and probably artificial super intelligence within the next five years. Uh, \",\"startTime\":1744724380,\"endTime\":1744724383},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"that''s my, my guess. \",\"startTime\":1744724383,\"endTime\":1744724386},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"And so based on that, like what do we need to be doing in a post sort of post knowledge work world, if you will? So I would say like. \",\"startTime\":1744724387,\"endTime\":1744724396},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"We need to be thinking about how do we build and maintain these systems. So \",\"startTime\":1744724396,\"endTime\":1744724400},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"I think like a return to like hardware and industrialization in in like a manner of speaking is like important. \",\"startTime\":1744724400,\"endTime\":1744724407},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"''Cause they have to build and fix these things.\",\"startTime\":1744724408,\"endTime\":1744724411},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"But also that changes knowledge work dramatically. Umm, we go from a world where \",\"startTime\":1744724411,\"endTime\":1744724415},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"it''s like you''re hired based on your expertise of like a content knowledge to maybe like how do you leverage that content or or augment your understandings with AI is, is probably what we really need to be thinking about. So how do \",\"startTime\":1744724415,\"endTime\":1744724427},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"we become problem seekers, not just problem solvers, but problem seekers. \",\"startTime\":1744724427,\"endTime\":1744724432},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"Umm, and how do we sort of, you know, yeah, I feel like we''re reaching kind of the next tier of like civilization. Like, what does that mean for? \",\"startTime\":1744724432,\"endTime\":1744724441},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"How do we build the new things to do the things we can''t even imagine right now? Creativity dreamers. \",\"startTime\":1744724442,\"endTime\":1744724448},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"Umm, I think umm.\",\"startTime\":1744724470,\"endTime\":1744724471},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"Probably the biggest struggle that that I''m facing at the moment is.\",\"startTime\":1744724471,\"endTime\":1744724476},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"I think sort of tempering speed.\",\"startTime\":1744724476,\"endTime\":1744724478},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"Like, I think we need to move faster. I don''t think we''re moving fast enough. \",\"startTime\":1744724479,\"endTime\":1744724482},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"Umm, but I also know that like, umm, that, that this is like, it''s like you''re not, you''re not steering a small boat or a dinghy with a little outboard motor. \",\"startTime\":1744724482,\"endTime\":1744724492},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"You''re steering a cruise ship. So you have to be thoughtful about how you maneuver. \",\"startTime\":1744724492,\"endTime\":1744724497},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"Umm. And so, yeah, I think we need to move faster. I think there needs to be \",\"startTime\":1744724498,\"endTime\":1744724501},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"an elevated sense of urgency. \",\"startTime\":1744724501,\"endTime\":1744724504},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"Umm, but I also know that, umm, there are systems and people and all sorts of things that have to move with that and so. \",\"startTime\":1744724504,\"endTime\":1744724512},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"Striking the right balance is challenging, and as you create more urgency, that also creates more. \",\"startTime\":1744724514,\"endTime\":1744724521},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"Push back more friction. So kind of dealing with some of those frictions is \",\"startTime\":1744724522,\"endTime\":1744724525},{\"speaker\":\"11981\",\"text\":\"a challenge too. \",\"startTime\":1744724525,\"endTime\":1744724527}]"', '2025-04-30 20:57:08.234362+00', '2025-04-30 20:57:08.234362+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 256, "created_at": "2025-04-30T20:57:08.200Z", "session_title": "#ai_learning_tools", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "190", "name": "#ai_learning_tools", "tags": [{"name": "Dream Camp"}, {"name": "AI in Education"}, {"name": "Freemium"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('2b3c65e3-5320-4045-babe-64909c58764f', '1437c66b-ec40-4d5f-ae09-61eaf239da58', '137222', '"[{\"speaker\":\"11895\",\"text\":\"Hi there. Right now I teach math and video production at the high school level, \",\"startTime\":1740111634,\"endTime\":1740111639},{\"speaker\":\"11895\",\"text\":\"and then I teach a lot of teachers and educators how to use artificial intelligence. \",\"startTime\":1740111639,\"endTime\":1740111643},{\"speaker\":\"11895\",\"text\":\"I teach primarily by facilitating conversation, not really by talking at people. \",\"startTime\":1740111645,\"endTime\":1740111649},{\"speaker\":\"11895\",\"text\":\"But I tend to push people to try things that. \",\"startTime\":1740111649,\"endTime\":1740111653},{\"speaker\":\"11895\",\"text\":\"They think might not work.\",\"startTime\":1740111653,\"endTime\":1740111654},{\"speaker\":\"11895\",\"text\":\"And I think that can be really helpful. So I''ll play the role of coach and.\",\"startTime\":1740111656,\"endTime\":1740111660},{\"speaker\":\"11895\",\"text\":\"Kind of cheerleader, just like it''s going to work.\",\"startTime\":1740111660,\"endTime\":1740111662},{\"speaker\":\"11895\",\"text\":\"And then we''ll laugh together if it doesn''t.\",\"startTime\":1740111663,\"endTime\":1740111665},{\"speaker\":\"11895\",\"text\":\"Is stolen from Jeff Crawford.\",\"startTime\":1740111682,\"endTime\":1740111684},{\"speaker\":\"11895\",\"text\":\"Position each learner is capable value the perspective of multiple learners and. \",\"startTime\":1740111684,\"endTime\":1740111689},{\"speaker\":\"11895\",\"text\":\"Enhance the identity and agency of each learner. That''s what I''m working an \",\"startTime\":1740111692,\"endTime\":1740111694},{\"speaker\":\"11895\",\"text\":\"aspiring. \",\"startTime\":1740111694,\"endTime\":1740111696},{\"speaker\":\"11895\",\"text\":\"To doing everything.\",\"startTime\":1740111697,\"endTime\":1740111699},{\"speaker\":\"11895\",\"text\":\"I''m also very inspired by or like my craft by the standards of math practice, the standards of practice versus. \",\"startTime\":1740111699,\"endTime\":1740111705},{\"speaker\":\"11895\",\"text\":\"Content standards.\",\"startTime\":1740111706,\"endTime\":1740111707},{\"speaker\":\"11895\",\"text\":\"And what else? I think there''s a better way to do things than the status quo. \",\"startTime\":1740111712,\"endTime\":1740111717},{\"speaker\":\"11895\",\"text\":\"I''m a skier.\",\"startTime\":1740111734,\"endTime\":1740111735},{\"speaker\":\"11895\",\"text\":\"Through and through.\",\"startTime\":1740111735,\"endTime\":1740111736},{\"speaker\":\"11895\",\"text\":\"Umm, I''m a big mountain skier so I like to ski on Umm.\",\"startTime\":1740111739,\"endTime\":1740111744},{\"speaker\":\"11895\",\"text\":\"Like not ungroomed runs, but like navigate through terrain and fun ways like jumping off of things, going around them. Umm, it''s just, it''s fast and it''s \",\"startTime\":1740111745,\"endTime\":1740111753},{\"speaker\":\"11895\",\"text\":\"fun and it works and it feels like it shouldn''t. \",\"startTime\":1740111753,\"endTime\":1740111758},{\"speaker\":\"11895\",\"text\":\"So I''m a skier.\",\"startTime\":1740111760,\"endTime\":1740111761}]"', '2025-04-30 20:57:08.243612+00', '2025-04-30 20:57:08.243612+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 108, "created_at": "2025-04-30T20:57:08.213Z", "session_title": "Welcome to sideby!", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "22", "name": "Welcome to sideby!", "tags": [{"name": "Active"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}, {"name": "Leaders of Color"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('9c47e747-d98d-460e-bbbc-be2c7a39271f', '44d8b840-888f-4849-9111-b52ada8f4599', '137151', '"[{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"My favorite futuristic movie that incorporates technology probably has to be the Minority Report. I think it was made in 2010 with Tom Cruise. That''s what \",\"startTime\":1739926547,\"endTime\":1739926556},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"it looks like. \",\"startTime\":1739926556,\"endTime\":1739926560},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"I really like this one because he uses his hands to kind of do an Apple Vision Pro. \",\"startTime\":1739926561,\"endTime\":1739926567},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"Vibe where he is controlling his monitor and what he''s searching through all by his hands. \",\"startTime\":1739926567,\"endTime\":1739926573},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"It is my absolute dream to I put on fun glasses or just pull up as a mini screens as possible in my space like an Apple Vision Pro. I remember seeing that and \",\"startTime\":1739926573,\"endTime\":1739926581},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"being like that''s my ideal study space. \",\"startTime\":1739926581,\"endTime\":1739926586},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"That''s where I want to work, so that''s probably my favorite movie.\",\"startTime\":1739926586,\"endTime\":1739926589},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"This is a good question. So AI has absolutely transformed my teaching practice \",\"startTime\":1739926608,\"endTime\":1739926612},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"with the main highlight that it has boosted my efficiency in getting tasks done as well has boosted my professional development and being able to reach and create. \",\"startTime\":1739926612,\"endTime\":1739926626},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"Items and resources to support all of my students.\",\"startTime\":1739926626,\"endTime\":1739926630},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"I have leveled up in my knowledge around supporting students with in special education with very particular exceptionalities. I have leveled up in my problem \",\"startTime\":1739926631,\"endTime\":1739926639},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"solving abilities in this new space as an educator, my ability to create resources and. \",\"startTime\":1739926639,\"endTime\":1739926647},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"Boost my productivity. I can do things so much faster and then in turn serve \",\"startTime\":1739926648,\"endTime\":1739926652},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"so many more students. \",\"startTime\":1739926652,\"endTime\":1739926656},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"This one is a hot topic right now in 2025. I do think that if I take it from \",\"startTime\":1739926682,\"endTime\":1739926686},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"my experience as a learner, I do think that AI is going to be such an incremental tool in helping learners. \",\"startTime\":1739926686,\"endTime\":1739926694},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"Learn new things and create things and just have access to doing.\",\"startTime\":1739926694,\"endTime\":1739926700},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"And being more and I also acknowledge that there is research that is showing that learners who over depend on that tool have lost a lot of that critical thinking skills. So I do think that it is an invaluable tool. \",\"startTime\":1739926700,\"endTime\":1739926715},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"With caution, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1739926716,\"endTime\":1739926717},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"Implementing an AI driven platform.\",\"startTime\":1739926751,\"endTime\":1739926752},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"Is going to serve all of my students, those with exceptionalities, those who are just coming into the school system, ELLMLS. \",\"startTime\":1739926752,\"endTime\":1739926759},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"You know, some of his parent teachers are concerned.\",\"startTime\":1739926762,\"endTime\":1739926764},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"How would this our concern that they are going to take over the it''s going to take over their jobs? Sorry, I was reading the question. How would I address \",\"startTime\":1739926764,\"endTime\":1739926771},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"these concerns? \",\"startTime\":1739926771,\"endTime\":1739926774},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"Great question.\",\"startTime\":1739926776,\"endTime\":1739926777},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"I think #1 is that.\",\"startTime\":1739926777,\"endTime\":1739926779},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"A robot cannot replace the social emotional skills, the perspective taking, the empathy, the relationship skills that people bring to the table. I cannot \",\"startTime\":1739926781,\"endTime\":1739926793},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"do that. I''m really thinking that reassuring them that, hey, this is not going \",\"startTime\":1739926793,\"endTime\":1739926799},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"to take over your job and it''s going to be a tool to help you. \",\"startTime\":1739926799,\"endTime\":1739926805},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"Be good at your not. It''s going to be a tool to help you.\",\"startTime\":1739926808,\"endTime\":1739926812},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"In your job, it''s gonna be a tool to help you in a job, kind of like, kind of like a weak analogy, but like a pencil is going to help you at work, This AI tool is going to also help you at work. It''s going to help you reach all students. \",\"startTime\":1739926813,\"endTime\":1739926827},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"I think this is what I might need to like really think about because I''m all in for AI. I''m like, yes, let''s do it. And I do acknowledge that there are some \",\"startTime\":1739926830,\"endTime\":1739926836},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"people that are like, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, new thing that''s scary. I''m not \",\"startTime\":1739926836,\"endTime\":1739926840},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"open to that right now and that''s totally fine. \",\"startTime\":1739926840,\"endTime\":1739926843},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"I think starting with acknowledging.\",\"startTime\":1739926844,\"endTime\":1739926846},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"Her feelings are reassuring and showing them like you are so valuable and this is not going to replace you when you adopt this. \",\"startTime\":1739926847,\"endTime\":1739926854},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"Then it''s going to help all students succeed, and that''s our main goal here. \",\"startTime\":1739926855,\"endTime\":1739926857},{\"speaker\":\"11883\",\"text\":\"So really centering it on what are our values and how can that tool help us get there? \",\"startTime\":1739926857,\"endTime\":1739926863}]"', '2025-04-30 20:57:08.465227+00', '2025-04-30 20:57:08.465227+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 260, "created_at": "2025-04-30T20:57:08.438Z", "session_title": "#ai_learning_tools", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "190", "name": "#ai_learning_tools", "tags": [{"name": "Dream Camp"}, {"name": "AI in Education"}, {"name": "Freemium"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
