	('efeb3924-6ee0-44dd-8ad6-7f146af95c8f', 'c9d72e87-97e2-4131-bf2e-7298453c0e52', '138222', '"[{\"speaker\":\"11999\",\"text\":\"Hello, my name is Mike Mendelsohn.\",\"startTime\":1745283431,\"endTime\":1745283434},{\"speaker\":\"11999\",\"text\":\"And I, umm, I''m one of those teachers here. I''m hoping to build it, umm.\",\"startTime\":1745283434,\"endTime\":1745283438},{\"speaker\":\"11999\",\"text\":\"I currently teach high school math in the last 8 weeks.\",\"startTime\":1745283443,\"endTime\":1745283446},{\"speaker\":\"11999\",\"text\":\"And.\",\"startTime\":1745283446,\"endTime\":1745283447},{\"speaker\":\"11999\",\"text\":\"I am excited about how much.\",\"startTime\":1745283449,\"endTime\":1745283451},{\"speaker\":\"11999\",\"text\":\"I''m excited at creating a a community where people can talk with each other and learn about each other''s perspective and how we''re all thinking so that we can all think a little faster together. \",\"startTime\":1745283456,\"endTime\":1745283470},{\"speaker\":\"11999\",\"text\":\"Uh, I I actually don''t care what I learn about. I hope everyone else here learns \",\"startTime\":1745283475,\"endTime\":1745283478},{\"speaker\":\"11999\",\"text\":\"a lot. \",\"startTime\":1745283478,\"endTime\":1745283481},{\"speaker\":\"11999\",\"text\":\"I''m sure that I will learn a lot.\",\"startTime\":1745283481,\"endTime\":1745283483},{\"speaker\":\"11999\",\"text\":\"But my job is to learn how to make it easier for you guys to learn.\",\"startTime\":1745283483,\"endTime\":1745283486},{\"speaker\":\"11999\",\"text\":\"My stance with respect to teaching and learning is that, umm, we should do more of it. \",\"startTime\":1745283502,\"endTime\":1745283508},{\"speaker\":\"11999\",\"text\":\"When we decide to learn something, we do and we get better and thus make the world better. When we decide to teach something, I don''t mean profess about \",\"startTime\":1745283512,\"endTime\":1745283519},{\"speaker\":\"11999\",\"text\":\"it, but I mean like take knowledge we have and. \",\"startTime\":1745283519,\"endTime\":1745283522},{\"speaker\":\"11999\",\"text\":\"Put it in someone else''s brain and make them more capable so we make the world better in that way as well. \",\"startTime\":1745283524,\"endTime\":1745283529},{\"speaker\":\"11999\",\"text\":\"My primary full activity is skiing, snow skiing. I like not to ski in a very \",\"startTime\":1745283543,\"endTime\":1745283547},{\"speaker\":\"11999\",\"text\":\"playful, exploratory way and one of the things that marks my skiing. \",\"startTime\":1745283547,\"endTime\":1745283552},{\"speaker\":\"11999\",\"text\":\"Is that I''m always either pointed straight downhill or in a traverse.\",\"startTime\":1745283552,\"endTime\":1745283557},{\"speaker\":\"11999\",\"text\":\"And I found that I can because of that I can find more fresh turns.\",\"startTime\":1745283558,\"endTime\":1745283561},{\"speaker\":\"11999\",\"text\":\"And I can.\",\"startTime\":1745283562,\"endTime\":1745283564},{\"speaker\":\"11999\",\"text\":\"Have more fun.\",\"startTime\":1745283567,\"endTime\":1745283568},{\"speaker\":\"11999\",\"text\":\"All the time.\",\"startTime\":1745283569,\"endTime\":1745283570},{\"speaker\":\"11999\",\"text\":\"I tend to stay off of trails and ski alone or with friends.\",\"startTime\":1745283570,\"endTime\":1745283576}]"', '2025-04-30 20:57:08.873025+00', '2025-04-30 20:57:08.873025+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 134, "created_at": "2025-04-30T20:57:08.827Z", "session_title": "Welcome to sideby!", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "22", "name": "Welcome to sideby!", "tags": [{"name": "Active"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}, {"name": "Leaders of Color"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('699f5e1b-e392-4e16-b46b-6f52451bba6c', '59e9f386-0ecc-4201-99dd-802f7f8e7b33', '138230', '"[{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Hi there, I''m Nova Katz and I''m a math coach. I specialize in supporting teachers \",\"startTime\":1745350408,\"endTime\":1745350413},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"with elementary math, and in particular I love talking about multiple representations in mathematics and supporting students with using manipulatives and connecting representations. \",\"startTime\":1745350413,\"endTime\":1745350426},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"My why is to decrease barriers to access.\",\"startTime\":1745350426,\"endTime\":1745350432},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Based on students math abilities and their beliefs in themselves.\",\"startTime\":1745350433,\"endTime\":1745350436},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Umm, I hope to learn about how other people are doing this work and how other people are, umm, supporting students with a growth mindset. \",\"startTime\":1745350437,\"endTime\":1745350446},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Umm, my stance is that everyone can. Just like we say that every student can \",\"startTime\":1745350477,\"endTime\":1745350482},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"learn math at very high levels and that every student should be appropriately challenged in math class umm, I also believe that every teacher can. So as a \",\"startTime\":1745350482,\"endTime\":1745350492},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"math coach, I work specifically with teachers. I believe that every teacher \",\"startTime\":1745350492,\"endTime\":1745350497},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"can teach math to high levels, and I believe that every teacher can meet the needs of every single learner in their class and I. \",\"startTime\":1745350497,\"endTime\":1745350506},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Empowering teachers to see that they have everything they already need within themselves. \",\"startTime\":1745350506,\"endTime\":1745350511},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"And I say that I get to do all of the research and reading that as teachers we don''t get time to do. And I bring to you what might be useful. \",\"startTime\":1745350512,\"endTime\":1745350519},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Things I do to flow include knitting.\",\"startTime\":1745350554,\"endTime\":1745350558},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"I love to knit, although I don''t I haven''t been knitting lately. I''ve also recently \",\"startTime\":1745350558,\"endTime\":1745350562},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"done pottery and I love spinning ceramics on the wheel. Umm, I definitely lose \",\"startTime\":1745350562,\"endTime\":1745350566},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"track of time when I''m doing that. \",\"startTime\":1745350566,\"endTime\":1745350570},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"And I also love playing games with my family, in particular games like Catan and Terraforming Mars. Really big bulky games that take a long time to play. \",\"startTime\":1745350570,\"endTime\":1745350577},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Those are really fun for me. \",\"startTime\":1745350577,\"endTime\":1745350581}]"', '2025-04-30 20:57:08.889751+00', '2025-04-30 20:57:08.889751+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 124, "created_at": "2025-04-30T20:57:08.860Z", "session_title": "Welcome to sideby!", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "22", "name": "Welcome to sideby!", "tags": [{"name": "Active"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}, {"name": "Leaders of Color"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('f838f2cf-0553-4e40-8671-aefc4a913571', '4bb175fe-ebd9-4641-9edc-593037b6152d', '138201', '"[{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"Hi, I''m Michelle and I am a science teacher by trade. I have done that for about \",\"startTime\":1745072027,\"endTime\":1745072031},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"20 years. \",\"startTime\":1745072031,\"endTime\":1745072033},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"But I''m also.\",\"startTime\":1745072033,\"endTime\":1745072034},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"Really proud to be a leader in my school. I do some instructional coaching and \",\"startTime\":1745072035,\"endTime\":1745072038},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"that''s my favorite work that I do right now is working with teachers to help improve their practice. \",\"startTime\":1745072038,\"endTime\":1745072044},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"And then I''ve also gotten to do a lot of work as an advisor to students in our crew structure. \",\"startTime\":1745072044,\"endTime\":1745072049},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"And something that I hope to learn about through this process is just a lot more about how to utilize AI to. \",\"startTime\":1745072050,\"endTime\":1745072059},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"Make the teaching process, the communication process better, easier for myself and then especially for the teachers that I work with, I want to understand the capabilities of that tool in order to make. \",\"startTime\":1745072062,\"endTime\":1745072076},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"To free up some capacity for teachers so that they can use their time.\",\"startTime\":1745072079,\"endTime\":1745072084},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"Hi, I''m Michelle coming to you from California. I am a science teacher, high \",\"startTime\":1745072117,\"endTime\":1745072122},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"school science teacher by trade, and also an advisor for students through our crew structure and then the work that I''ve done over the past few years that I have really fallen in love with and where my energy is going. \",\"startTime\":1745072122,\"endTime\":1745072135},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"Umm, in. The biggest way right now is toward coaching teachers as an instructional \",\"startTime\":1745072135,\"endTime\":1745072136},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"guide. \",\"startTime\":1745072136,\"endTime\":1745072138},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"And what I''m hoping to learn through this process is specifically a lot more about AI and what its capabilities are. \",\"startTime\":1745072141,\"endTime\":1745072151},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"Within education and.\",\"startTime\":1745072151,\"endTime\":1745072153},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"Both for myself from when I''m in Pasadena as a teacher, but also.\",\"startTime\":1745072153,\"endTime\":1745072158},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"CS GO awful hate it.\",\"startTime\":1745072161,\"endTime\":1745072162},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"Hi, I''m Michelle. I am a high school science teacher from California. I also \",\"startTime\":1745072182,\"endTime\":1745072188},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"do some crew advising and work as an instructional guide coaching teachers. \",\"startTime\":1745072188,\"endTime\":1745072193},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"And I hope through this process to learn a lot more from.\",\"startTime\":1745072193,\"endTime\":1745072198},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"Peers about what the potential is to utilize AI.\",\"startTime\":1745072199,\"endTime\":1745072203},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"Umm, to make a really challenging job, uh.\",\"startTime\":1745072205,\"endTime\":1745072208},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"More efficient, more impactful and to help growth for myself when I am in teaching capacity, use it to improve and support my lesson design and then when I''m in a coaching capacity, when I''m working with teachers. \",\"startTime\":1745072209,\"endTime\":1745072224},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"And especially those who are feeling just really overburdened by the workload to figure out how we can use technology to. \",\"startTime\":1745072224,\"endTime\":1745072231},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"Lift off some of that weight and do some of the work.\",\"startTime\":1745072232,\"endTime\":1745072236},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"Umm, for them?\",\"startTime\":1745072236,\"endTime\":1745072238},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"So that they can concentrate their expertise in other areas that are maybe more directly helping students, leave them with a little more energy for the good work that they have to do. \",\"startTime\":1745072238,\"endTime\":1745072247},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"My stance with respect, teaching and learning.\",\"startTime\":1745072513,\"endTime\":1745072515},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"It''s hard to capture in one minute. I have a lot to say about that, but if I \",\"startTime\":1745072515,\"endTime\":1745072517},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"boiled it down. \",\"startTime\":1745072517,\"endTime\":1745072520},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"I would say that the job of a teacher is to ask great questions to.\",\"startTime\":1745072520,\"endTime\":1745072525},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"Create or curate resources for students to create the conditions for learning. \",\"startTime\":1745072527,\"endTime\":1745072533},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"And to model curiosity for students.\",\"startTime\":1745072533,\"endTime\":1745072536},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"And then the job of the students is to do the work. They should be the ones \",\"startTime\":1745072536,\"endTime\":1745072539},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"working hard. They should be the ones feeling. \",\"startTime\":1745072539,\"endTime\":1745072542},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"Challenged in class they.\",\"startTime\":1745072543,\"endTime\":1745072546},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"Should be the ones talking especially to each other, using each other as resources and then they also should be asking. \",\"startTime\":1745072547,\"endTime\":1745072553},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"Good questions, hard questions, and seeking the answers, often with guidance from the teacher and support from their peers as well. \",\"startTime\":1745072554,\"endTime\":1745072562},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"I have two main flow activities that come to mind. The 1st is running which. \",\"startTime\":1745072600,\"endTime\":1745072604},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"To say it takes me the 1st 10 minutes or so usually not in the flow but I think. \",\"startTime\":1745072604,\"endTime\":1745072609},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"Push myself beyond that the next.\",\"startTime\":1745072609,\"endTime\":1745072611},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"Sometimes hours. So it feels really good about having a good day. Umm And then \",\"startTime\":1745072612,\"endTime\":1745072616},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"the other thing that I can really get lost in and really enjoy doing is is cooking. \",\"startTime\":1745072616,\"endTime\":1745072621},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"So making dinner for myself and my family. \",\"startTime\":1745072621,\"endTime\":1745072625},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"Umm, especially if I can have the kitchen and the space all to myself. And maybe \",\"startTime\":1745072626,\"endTime\":1745072629},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"if I can also. \",\"startTime\":1745072629,\"endTime\":1745072631},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"Pop in some headphones and watch a show, some junky show, while I am chopping and sauteing and cooking up something delicious. That''s something that. \",\"startTime\":1745072631,\"endTime\":1745072640},{\"speaker\":\"11995\",\"text\":\"I really look forward to and can get lost in in my daily routine.\",\"startTime\":1745072641,\"endTime\":1745072645}]"', '2025-04-30 20:57:08.447439+00', '2025-04-30 20:57:08.447439+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 178, "created_at": "2025-04-30T20:57:08.430Z", "session_title": "Welcome to sideby!", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "22", "name": "Welcome to sideby!", "tags": [{"name": "Active"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}, {"name": "Leaders of Color"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('e46f7b23-8ce0-47c6-b187-65b00ca2565a', 'e6a3a52f-5383-4756-9c91-2b4068ee26e3', '138316', '"[{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"Hi my name is Joseph Marvie. I am currently a middle school math teacher teaching \",\"startTime\":1745632283,\"endTime\":1745632286},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"7th and 8th grades and. \",\"startTime\":1745632286,\"endTime\":1745632289},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"I have a history of teaching elementary, middle, and high school.\",\"startTime\":1745632289,\"endTime\":1745632293},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"I''ve had a significant amount of experience with curriculum instruction, uh, kind of coaching uh, teachers through organizations like uh, National Math and Science Initiative and its illustrative mathematics. But throughout this time, \",\"startTime\":1745632293,\"endTime\":1745632306},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"I''ve been pretty invested in Ed tech. In fact, my own uh, background is in technology \",\"startTime\":1745632306,\"endTime\":1745632311},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"and, uh, kind of in the technology background. \",\"startTime\":1745632311,\"endTime\":1745632315},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"And that kind of path naturally took me.\",\"startTime\":1745632317,\"endTime\":1745632321},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"To kind of AI about five years ago and there''s been a lot of work that we''ve done. What I''m really curious about is how do we use AI right now? That''s been \",\"startTime\":1745632321,\"endTime\":1745632329},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"something that''s on my mind. \",\"startTime\":1745632329,\"endTime\":1745632333},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"So how do we use AI from a kind of a learner perspective, right, Where the learner first and the solution like all these AI solutions later. So how do we use AI \",\"startTime\":1745632335,\"endTime\":1745632346},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"to kind of create equity access and present high quality learning materials for that make accessibility both manageable for both the teacher and the student and also make sure that you are not compromising the relations. \",\"startTime\":1745632346,\"endTime\":1745632364},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"Between the student and the teacher, so that it''s not just, you know, technology focus. \",\"startTime\":1745632364,\"endTime\":1745632369},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"Umm, yeah. So that''s kind of my interest in kind of pursuing with the AI path \",\"startTime\":1745632369,\"endTime\":1745632372},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"right now. \",\"startTime\":1745632372,\"endTime\":1745632374},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"Uh, my name is Yusuf. Uh, I''m currently a middle school math teacher.\",\"startTime\":1745632390,\"endTime\":1745632394},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"Teaching 8th grade, that''s that''s my full time kind of job.\",\"startTime\":1745632394,\"endTime\":1745632399},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"In addition to it, I''m pretty heavily invested within my district kind of thinking about what AI looks like both in terms of just another technology, but in terms of. \",\"startTime\":1745632400,\"endTime\":1745632411},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"You know the AI policies. I''m a member of the AI Academic Honesty Committee. \",\"startTime\":1745632411,\"endTime\":1745632416},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"Which is trying to create like kind of a protocol and a guideline for the school district of 30,000 about what engagement both from a learning teacher perspective looks like. I also work pretty intensely with the school district and trying \",\"startTime\":1745632417,\"endTime\":1745632432},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"to onboard the first student facing AI. \",\"startTime\":1745632432,\"endTime\":1745632437},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"Product for the school district, which has gone great.\",\"startTime\":1745632438,\"endTime\":1745632442},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"So right now what''s on my mind and what I''m really trying to learn about is how do we use AI to create access? \",\"startTime\":1745632443,\"endTime\":1745632450},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"And at the same time bring rigorous learning without compromising the relationship between the student and the teacher. Not just like the student teacher relationship, \",\"startTime\":1745632451,\"endTime\":1745632461},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"but but also where the teacher is a facilitator of the learning. \",\"startTime\":1745632461,\"endTime\":1745632465},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"So not just, you know, printing worksheets, having more worksheets in the name of differentiation, but, uh. \",\"startTime\":1745632465,\"endTime\":1745632470},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"Yeah, so kind of really add that Nexus of.\",\"startTime\":1745632471,\"endTime\":1745632475},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"Make How do we use this technology for creating a more equitable learning environment without compromising the rigor and the quality of the education at the same time? \",\"startTime\":1745632476,\"endTime\":1745632489},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"Managing the teacher student relationship and actually using AI to deepen that rather than compromising that. \",\"startTime\":1745632490,\"endTime\":1745632498},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"Umm, So as I think about umm, what you know, the stance in terms of teaching and learning? \",\"startTime\":1745632538,\"endTime\":1745632544},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"Avoid the tropes about, you know, the facilitator and things like that. And \",\"startTime\":1745632544,\"endTime\":1745632548},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"they''re 100% true. A teacher is a facilitator. \",\"startTime\":1745632548,\"endTime\":1745632552},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"But I think where I my stance is in terms of the role of the teacher and the student is that as part of the spectrum, right? What the student teacher relationship \",\"startTime\":1745632552,\"endTime\":1745632560},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"looks like in one environment. So I worked in Title 1 environments is really \",\"startTime\":1745632560,\"endTime\":1745632564},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"highly populations. And I''m currently in a environment where it would be considered \",\"startTime\":1745632564,\"endTime\":1745632569},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"privileged environment. That relationship looks very different. Regardless, \",\"startTime\":1745632569,\"endTime\":1745632573},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"in all those environments, my job is to make the learning happen, right? So, \",\"startTime\":1745632573,\"endTime\":1745632577},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"and that happens with the. \",\"startTime\":1745632577,\"endTime\":1745632581},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"In between the completely understanding a the needs of the student and the community and the aspirations of the community and where the learning that you are responsible for fits in And what do you what role do you play in making it happen? \",\"startTime\":1745632583,\"endTime\":1745632599},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"So that that''s what I really think. I think it''s, it''s all within a spectrum, \",\"startTime\":1745632600,\"endTime\":1745632605},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"but fundamentally teacher is making responsible for finding ways for that learning to happen to have the transformational change, not just within a student, but within that, that the family and hopefully in the larger community as well. \",\"startTime\":1745632605,\"endTime\":1745632619},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"I think what should change is I don''t think. \",\"startTime\":1745632619,\"endTime\":1745632623},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"Much should change in the sense of what I hope a teaching experience looks like, but I do think what it should like look like is. \",\"startTime\":1745632624,\"endTime\":1745632632},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"More ways that a teacher becomes that role model or that conduit for that connection. \",\"startTime\":1745632633,\"endTime\":1745632638},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"Umm, and in terms of technology for that to do so, it can do all of it, but whatever role it plays. \",\"startTime\":1745632638,\"endTime\":1745632647},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"I''m just really excited to see what that could look like, especially in terms of instruction. It can do maybe the relationship, but it can definitely facilitate. \",\"startTime\":1745632649,\"endTime\":1745632656},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"The equity and accessibility of that instruction, and as I mentioned, what should stay the same, is that the where the teacher fits in that spectrum of how learning happens. \",\"startTime\":1745632657,\"endTime\":1745632668},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"Although I, I, it would be kind of hypocritical for me to accept it because I don''t get to do it as often. But there are very few things that kind of get \",\"startTime\":1745632701,\"endTime\":1745632709},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"me going as like even a, a, a mile or two mile run. So I was saying my flow \",\"startTime\":1745632709,\"endTime\":1745632714},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"activity would be running because it really helps me reset. It really brings \",\"startTime\":1745632714,\"endTime\":1745632718},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"up my energy levels. Something as small as a one mile run can really kind of \",\"startTime\":1745632718,\"endTime\":1745632722},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"change how my day is going. So I, I, I, I as much as I can, I, I would love \",\"startTime\":1745632722,\"endTime\":1745632726},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"to be outside. \",\"startTime\":1745632726,\"endTime\":1745632730},{\"speaker\":\"12020\",\"text\":\"I don''t get to do it that much, but I''ve been much better at it in the last two months and I hope to continue that. \",\"startTime\":1745632730,\"endTime\":1745632736}]"', '2025-04-30 20:57:08.797969+00', '2025-04-30 20:57:08.797969+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 287, "created_at": "2025-04-30T20:57:08.775Z", "session_title": "Welcome to sideby!", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "22", "name": "Welcome to sideby!", "tags": [{"name": "Active"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}, {"name": "Leaders of Color"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('da3d477d-1f80-4d1f-acaa-d34c9bffe9b5', 'c9d72e87-97e2-4131-bf2e-7298453c0e52', '137943', '"[]"', '2025-04-30 20:57:08.858831+00', '2025-04-30 20:57:08.858831+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 45, "created_at": "2025-04-30T20:57:08.841Z", "session_title": "Welcome to sideby!", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "22", "name": "Welcome to sideby!", "tags": [{"name": "Active"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}, {"name": "Leaders of Color"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('f60c8474-b212-4c81-927a-938757746564', 'db53cc1a-13b8-41ef-bc7c-401cd5851e20', '137348', '"[{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Hello, My name''s Jeff Crawford.\",\"startTime\":1740784077,\"endTime\":1740784078},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"And I''m an educator who loves to facilitate learning. I think of myself as one \",\"startTime\":1740784078,\"endTime\":1740784084},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"who enjoys getting people to think and talk about things, whether that''s putting them in conversations with each other or engaging with tasks problems. \",\"startTime\":1740784084,\"endTime\":1740784096},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Or something that''s even like a project that''s important and big.\",\"startTime\":1740784099,\"endTime\":1740784103},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Where they''re put in a position.\",\"startTime\":1740784104,\"endTime\":1740784107},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"That they have to try something or think about something differently than they''ve ever done before. \",\"startTime\":1740784109,\"endTime\":1740784114},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"That is, I feel like I''m a.\",\"startTime\":1740784115,\"endTime\":1740784116},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Budding neuroscientist who''s learned that education is all about cultivating the brain. \",\"startTime\":1740784119,\"endTime\":1740784125},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"And I think of humans and the chemicals and the stuff that happens in our brain, and I want to help each learner at each stage in their life to grow. \",\"startTime\":1740784126,\"endTime\":1740784135},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"And currently.\",\"startTime\":1740784136,\"endTime\":1740784137},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"What I hope to learn about through this time.\",\"startTime\":1740784137,\"endTime\":1740784139},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"With side by is to enjoy the richness of other people''s perspective so that I might get clearer on what I can do and how I can grow to be better when I''m an educator in any situation, whether it''s online writing through e-mail or text, or some messaging. \",\"startTime\":1740784140,\"endTime\":1740784159},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Or whether I''m facilitating in person, I want to get better.\",\"startTime\":1740784161,\"endTime\":1740784164},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"My stance is that each learner is capable of figuring things out on their own. \",\"startTime\":1740784202,\"endTime\":1740784210},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"That the role of the teacher.\",\"startTime\":1740784211,\"endTime\":1740784213},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Is to create a safe place.\",\"startTime\":1740784213,\"endTime\":1740784215},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"For each learner to feel one where they are positioned as capable.\",\"startTime\":1740784215,\"endTime\":1740784221},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"And two, that they have an identity, an agency that''s valuable.\",\"startTime\":1740784223,\"endTime\":1740784229},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"And that three, that there''s other perspectives that are wonderful that would help their thinking, and that their own thinking in ways of doing things would help others. \",\"startTime\":1740784229,\"endTime\":1740784238},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"I believe the role of the the teacher is rather a facilitator of learning.\",\"startTime\":1740784239,\"endTime\":1740784243},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"And the role of the student is to press themselves as far as they can to do things that that are beyond what they''ve even imagined doing before, Like a little child who''s learning to walk or talk, They stumble through it. I think \",\"startTime\":1740784243,\"endTime\":1740784256},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"that''s the role of the learner, And the role of the teacher is to encourage them and gently guide them. \",\"startTime\":1740784256,\"endTime\":1740784264},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"And provide tasks and opportunities in safe places.\",\"startTime\":1740784267,\"endTime\":1740784271},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Where they can get out of their survival mode in their brain and they know that they have value and belonging in whatever community or group or space that they''re in and that they can grow. And that role as a facilitator is to help learners \",\"startTime\":1740784271,\"endTime\":1740784285},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"engage and feel welcome and invited into the learning to stimulate their challenge, their task. \",\"startTime\":1740784285,\"endTime\":1740784294},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"Their way of thinking beyond what they''ve done before.\",\"startTime\":1740784297,\"endTime\":1740784301},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"And then to help the learner to synthesize their learning.\",\"startTime\":1740784303,\"endTime\":1740784306},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"I enjoy climbing rock climbing, whether it''s bouldering down low with no ropes in a crash pad below me. \",\"startTime\":1740784325,\"endTime\":1740784332},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"In the gym or outside or on a rope where I have safety gear and I''m up high. \",\"startTime\":1740784332,\"endTime\":1740784338},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"I enjoy the climbing, especially when it''s a new route or a problem that I''ve never done before. I find myself hyper focused. \",\"startTime\":1740784340,\"endTime\":1740784350},{\"speaker\":\"11912\",\"text\":\"In feeling and enjoying the rock and the rest of the world goes away.\",\"startTime\":1740784350,\"endTime\":1740784354}]"', '2025-04-30 20:57:08.934134+00', '2025-04-30 20:57:08.934134+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 243, "created_at": "2025-04-30T20:57:08.893Z", "session_title": "Welcome to sideby!", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "22", "name": "Welcome to sideby!", "tags": [{"name": "Active"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}, {"name": "Leaders of Color"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('36f9c35c-f2b2-47a1-b0d5-9de8fa2a6af2', 'db53cc1a-13b8-41ef-bc7c-401cd5851e20', '138134', '"[{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm.\",\"startTime\":1744664452,\"endTime\":1744664453},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Is that avocado toast?\",\"startTime\":1744664453,\"endTime\":1744664454},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"You''re always in the car. I''m sorry, I''m in the middle of eating lunch with \",\"startTime\":1744664453,\"endTime\":1744664455},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"my mom. \",\"startTime\":1744664455,\"endTime\":1744664458},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"No worries, no worries. I''m not always in the car, but lately, yes, a lot.\",\"startTime\":1744664459,\"endTime\":1744664463},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Just between things.\",\"startTime\":1744664464,\"endTime\":1744664465},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Is it moving?\",\"startTime\":1744664464,\"endTime\":1744664467},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Oh, it''s moving, dropping stuff off and we took a load of goodwill and my wife said she wanted to go and this is the time of the day at work. I''m like, but \",\"startTime\":1744664466,\"endTime\":1744664472},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I have a 2:00. \",\"startTime\":1744664472,\"endTime\":1744664475},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"So we get to, we get to chat this way.\",\"startTime\":1744664476,\"endTime\":1744664478},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"No, this counts.\",\"startTime\":1744664478,\"endTime\":1744664480},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"I don''t count.\",\"startTime\":1744664479,\"endTime\":1744664480},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"No. I mean it counts, but I don''t care if you''re in the car. You could call \",\"startTime\":1744664481,\"endTime\":1744664484},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"me from like a forest and I wouldn''t care. You know what I mean? \",\"startTime\":1744664484,\"endTime\":1744664487},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I know, I know. I hear you there. Oh, how are you today?\",\"startTime\":1744664488,\"endTime\":1744664492},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Good, I''m home visiting my family.\",\"startTime\":1744664494,\"endTime\":1744664495},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"This is my last meeting of the day, and then I think I''m gonna take a little time and, umm, go walk my dog in a park and stuff and like, hang out. \",\"startTime\":1744664496,\"endTime\":1744664503},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Good for you, good for you.\",\"startTime\":1744664503,\"endTime\":1744664505},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And where is home with family?\",\"startTime\":1744664506,\"endTime\":1744664508},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Yeah, wait, Petaluma, CA.\",\"startTime\":1744664506,\"endTime\":1744664509},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"OK, got you.\",\"startTime\":1744664509,\"endTime\":1744664510},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Wait, so I''ve greeted you then press more?\",\"startTime\":1744664513,\"endTime\":1744664517},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"I was just killed.\",\"startTime\":1744664518,\"endTime\":1744664519},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Oh my God, AI has totally changed my whole life.\",\"startTime\":1744664521,\"endTime\":1744664523},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Nice. What''s one way?\",\"startTime\":1744664523,\"endTime\":1744664527},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Honestly, I can do a lot more. Oh, actually, the most meaningful way that it''s \",\"startTime\":1744664529,\"endTime\":1744664532},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"changed my life actually does mean a lot to me. \",\"startTime\":1744664532,\"endTime\":1744664535},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"In a in a pre AI creating like structured deliverables and like plans like for people was really hard for me. Like a huge part of my job is like, excuse me, \",\"startTime\":1744664536,\"endTime\":1744664544},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"sorry. \",\"startTime\":1744664544,\"endTime\":1744664548},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"A huge part of my job is creating like structural structured content plans. \",\"startTime\":1744664550,\"endTime\":1744664553},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"So it''s like I like or, or deliverables like that where like I engage with a client, I learn about them and I need to make recommendations for them to like do a bunch of things. And I''m just always, my brain has always struggled to \",\"startTime\":1744664553,\"endTime\":1744664564},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"organize information. \",\"startTime\":1744664564,\"endTime\":1744664568},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"In that way, I just want to talk to people and I want to tell them things and I want to share things with them. I''ve always struggled to translate my raw \",\"startTime\":1744664570,\"endTime\":1744664575},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"thought into like. \",\"startTime\":1744664575,\"endTime\":1744664578},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Structure formatted deliverable, my raw talk dump thing and then ask AI to put it into a structured format for me and it will. And it''s like and it looks so \",\"startTime\":1744664583,\"endTime\":1744664592},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"good and it it''s so fast and it makes communication with my clients so easy and I''m just so grateful for that. \",\"startTime\":1744664592,\"endTime\":1744664600},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Oh, that is so.\",\"startTime\":1744664600,\"endTime\":1744664602},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"What about you?\",\"startTime\":1744664601,\"endTime\":1744664602},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"That''s hilarious because I''m doing almost the same type of thing. My day-to-day \",\"startTime\":1744664603,\"endTime\":1744664607},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"biggest win is I am. \",\"startTime\":1744664607,\"endTime\":1744664610},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And I did it because and I even did a post and I said.\",\"startTime\":1744664612,\"endTime\":1744664614},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Adding structure. Whose job is it? And I just got my thoughts out on, uh, what \",\"startTime\":1744664617,\"endTime\":1744664622},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I was thinking. And that''s my general thing I''ve been doing in my day-to-day. \",\"startTime\":1744664622,\"endTime\":1744664626},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Uh, I''ll use my Otter or some robot to record or just hit record on my phone. \",\"startTime\":1744664626,\"endTime\":1744664630},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And then from there I''ll record and then take and dump that into one of my robots. \",\"startTime\":1744664630,\"endTime\":1744664634},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And umm, it was great because it''s just taking and adding structure. And that \",\"startTime\":1744664634,\"endTime\":1744664638},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"was, that was my reflection even at the time, which is like now double meta is that. \",\"startTime\":1744664638,\"endTime\":1744664646},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I''m using it and I can let go of the, you know, like when you''re writing a book, for example, or blog post. \",\"startTime\":1744664648,\"endTime\":1744664654},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"MMM.\",\"startTime\":1744664650,\"endTime\":1744664651},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Or five paragraph paper when the way that we learn, like I learn in high school was here''s the title. And then you need to have your internal paragraph and \",\"startTime\":1744664656,\"endTime\":1744664663},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"then you have your main thesis and then you need to have three paragraphs and you''re like, Oh, I don''t know what my main thesis is that structure, the title or the, the thing we get hung up on that because it comes linearly first. And \",\"startTime\":1744664663,\"endTime\":1744664674},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1744664666,\"endTime\":1744664666},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"so I''ve been letting go of that structure and just talking and getting like you said, you want to have conversations. So I''ll be chatting with my AI bots \",\"startTime\":1744664674,\"endTime\":1744664682},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"by just like hitting. \",\"startTime\":1744664682,\"endTime\":1744664685},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Forward and getting the transcript and sometimes I''ll do it straight into the AI bot but I like it better. \",\"startTime\":1744664685,\"endTime\":1744664691},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"As I''m driving or walking, I''ll just be like reflection, thinking and talking about something because I know I go all over the place. And then I''m letting \",\"startTime\":1744664691,\"endTime\":1744664699},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"go of the wondering about the structure, like you said, about what the title is or what The thing is. And then I let it get some cool stuff out of it and \",\"startTime\":1744664699,\"endTime\":1744664707},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"then help me to move to structure. And if I know the structure already, then \",\"startTime\":1744664707,\"endTime\":1744664711},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I get there. But like what you''re saying. So that was really similar. \",\"startTime\":1744664711,\"endTime\":1744664715},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"It''s so helpful. I just have such raw dialogue brain and it''s so hard for me \",\"startTime\":1744664716,\"endTime\":1744664720},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"to put it into anyways. OK, do we? \",\"startTime\":1744664720,\"endTime\":1744664724},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah, same thing.\",\"startTime\":1744664725,\"endTime\":1744664726},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"That''s a fun fact about me too. Would you call it something dialogue brain? \",\"startTime\":1744664727,\"endTime\":1744664730},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Raw dialogue brain? \",\"startTime\":1744664730,\"endTime\":1744664733},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Wait, write dialogue frame and hit OK.\",\"startTime\":1744664733,\"endTime\":1744664736},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah, alright. What are some things that shape how you learn?\",\"startTime\":1744664737,\"endTime\":1744664741},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Umm, do you answer or do I answer?\",\"startTime\":1744664743,\"endTime\":1744664746},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Ask your partner. So I''m asking you, what are some things, some things cast \",\"startTime\":1744664747,\"endTime\":1744664750},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"that shape how you learn? \",\"startTime\":1744664750,\"endTime\":1744664753},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"How the information is presented to me and also experience. I''m so sensitive \",\"startTime\":1744664755,\"endTime\":1744664760},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"to how somebody presents information if I get the slightest whiff that they''re trying to convince me or I feel manipulated and become hostile to receiving information. I''m so aware that I function this way emotionally. If somebody \",\"startTime\":1744664760,\"endTime\":1744664773},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1744664761,\"endTime\":1744664761},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"presents something to me with like. \",\"startTime\":1744664773,\"endTime\":1744664778},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Intellectual humility where they''re like, well, this is what I think and it''s because of this. And then I read this and it like if they kind of like are really \",\"startTime\":1744664780,\"endTime\":1744664785},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"good at. \",\"startTime\":1744664785,\"endTime\":1744664788},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Being like I think this and This is why and there and I''m like very receptive to it. But if someone is conveying information to me in a way where I can tell \",\"startTime\":1744664788,\"endTime\":1744664795},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"their. \",\"startTime\":1744664795,\"endTime\":1744664798},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"They have an agenda about wanting me to believe it or just like there''s a you know what I mean? There''s a way of presenting information where I. \",\"startTime\":1744664802,\"endTime\":1744664808},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"If I feel manipulated by someone, I immediately just don''t believe anything they say. And it''s like rhetorical strategies, certain rhetorical strategies. \",\"startTime\":1744664810,\"endTime\":1744664817},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"That people will employ to seem confident or to be convincing can trigger that feeling in me and then I just won''t believe them instead of and like I''m trying to get better about that instead of just being like, no. \",\"startTime\":1744664818,\"endTime\":1744664831},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I like it. I like it on press on with your ideas that the question is what are \",\"startTime\":1744664833,\"endTime\":1744664838},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"some things that shape how you learn? You''re talking about people and their \",\"startTime\":1744664838,\"endTime\":1744664842},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"transparency or manipulation. \",\"startTime\":1744664842,\"endTime\":1744664846},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"What about when it comes to learning tech like tech tools like How is technology shape you? \",\"startTime\":1744664846,\"endTime\":1744664853},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"It''s oh, just have to.\",\"startTime\":1744664850,\"endTime\":1744664852},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"I just I just.\",\"startTime\":1744664853,\"endTime\":1744664855},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"I don''t, I mean is the question how tech using technology is shaped how I learn? \",\"startTime\":1744664857,\"endTime\":1744664862},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Or is it how do I learn new technology? \",\"startTime\":1744664862,\"endTime\":1744664867},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah. Or how, how, how is technology shaped your identity as a learner? That''s \",\"startTime\":1744664866,\"endTime\":1744664869},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"the question. \",\"startTime\":1744664869,\"endTime\":1744664872},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"It''s so hard for me to say because I''ve been using tech as long as I''ve been conscious. My dad put a computer in my room when I was like 6. \",\"startTime\":1744664872,\"endTime\":1744664881},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"And I''ve always, and I was like using an apple too when I was like barely able to write sentences. And I just never haven''t had. \",\"startTime\":1744664881,\"endTime\":1744664890},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"I, I, I don''t know. I have no idea. There''s no before and after in my life. \",\"startTime\":1744664893,\"endTime\":1744664895},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"I don''t know. \",\"startTime\":1744664895,\"endTime\":1744664897},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Well, when you think about that is, is that like partner tool right there with you so long in your life? How do you think that that''s shaped who you are as \",\"startTime\":1744664899,\"endTime\":1744664906},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"a learner or how you see yourself as a learner? \",\"startTime\":1744664906,\"endTime\":1744664910},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Hmm, I guess it''s made me not believe things at face value and want to explore them more always. I always assume there''s more to know because I have always \",\"startTime\":1744664917,\"endTime\":1744664928},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"had this connection to more resources that was very accessible to me. \",\"startTime\":1744664928,\"endTime\":1744664934},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"So instead of someone says something and I''m like OK and believe them, I''m like, oh, that could be true for you and then I''ll just keep looking for more. \",\"startTime\":1744664935,\"endTime\":1744664945},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Which I think is annoying to people, but.\",\"startTime\":1744664946,\"endTime\":1744664948},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I like it.\",\"startTime\":1744664947,\"endTime\":1744664947},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"No, I think some people really appreciate that and enjoy it and I think others are catching up. Maybe they didn''t grow up with one in their their their little \",\"startTime\":1744664953,\"endTime\":1744664958},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"kid bedroom. \",\"startTime\":1744664958,\"endTime\":1744664961},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Yeah, my dad was a very early adopter of computers.\",\"startTime\":1744664961,\"endTime\":1744664964},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Oh, that''s cool, that''s cool.\",\"startTime\":1744664965,\"endTime\":1744664966},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"What are some things that shape how you learn? Or do we just do you tell me \",\"startTime\":1744664967,\"endTime\":1744664968},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"All right, I''m first.\",\"startTime\":1744664967,\"endTime\":1744664968},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"no. \",\"startTime\":1744664968,\"endTime\":1744664970},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I don''t know what to say on yours.\",\"startTime\":1744664971,\"endTime\":1744664972},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Mine says the same thing as yours, so we both got the same instructions which makes it. \",\"startTime\":1744664973,\"endTime\":1744664977},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"That makes me wanna. Oh, that''s just a back and forth then, OK.\",\"startTime\":1744664978,\"endTime\":1744664982},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1744664982,\"endTime\":1744664983},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Shaping my learning.\",\"startTime\":1744664984,\"endTime\":1744664985},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I think it''s a lot of those experiences even with technology and AI tools that I can go faster with technology. Like you were just mentioned, writing out that \",\"startTime\":1744664987,\"endTime\":1744664995},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Lesson plan or the slide deck construct or whatever it is like that''s been super helpful even in the. \",\"startTime\":1744664995,\"endTime\":1744665003},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Copying and pasting or having files or building a template or organizing things, it feels like I can. \",\"startTime\":1744665005,\"endTime\":1744665011},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"It shapes how I learn is that I can step back and know that it''s already saved and I don''t have to remember it all and then and now even that helps create the structure, even file systems or way to organize my thinking. It helps me \",\"startTime\":1744665012,\"endTime\":1744665021},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"to organize my thinking. \",\"startTime\":1744665021,\"endTime\":1744665024},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I think that''s a huge component, but I think along the way it''s been, and you alluded to this is new things and trying it and testing it has put me at that learner position of I''m going to fail a lot and I''m going to break stuff and it''s going to crash. And I don''t know what''s going to really happen. I don''t \",\"startTime\":1744665024,\"endTime\":1744665039},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Cool.\",\"startTime\":1744665039,\"endTime\":1744665039},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"know how to use it yet, but I, I don''t even have an idea. And I''m guessing it''s, \",\"startTime\":1744665039,\"endTime\":1744665043},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"it''s big like your number would be of how many new apps or new programs that we''ve learned or try to assimilate. And then like you''ve gone down that path \",\"startTime\":1744665043,\"endTime\":1744665050},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"of, oh, it''s. \",\"startTime\":1744665050,\"endTime\":1744665054},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Program. It''s a new thing and a new system, a new whatever.\",\"startTime\":1744665057,\"endTime\":1744665059},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"New e-mail, all of that. So I think that shaped me a lot and somewhat it''s put \",\"startTime\":1744665059,\"endTime\":1744665063},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"me a little bit jaded. Now I''m finding like, oh, come on, don''t do that to me. \",\"startTime\":1744665063,\"endTime\":1744665066},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah, it was not in 1984. Seriously, folks. \",\"startTime\":1744665066,\"endTime\":1744665070},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1744665071,\"endTime\":1744665073},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Umm, because I''ve had had a lot of that experience, but also allows me to.\",\"startTime\":1744665072,\"endTime\":1744665075},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Easily adapt to I think new programs or tech stuff and.\",\"startTime\":1744665076,\"endTime\":1744665080},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Shaped how I learn is that I also I don''t want to be inquisitive. I want problems \",\"startTime\":1744665081,\"endTime\":1744665084},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"in front of me. I want to use new tools to figure it out and do new things. \",\"startTime\":1744665084,\"endTime\":1744665086},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I think that''s a. \",\"startTime\":1744665086,\"endTime\":1744665089},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"I, I see now also I can click more and there''s like these additional, there''s additional ideas and the question that I didn''t see before. Sorry, I didn''t \",\"startTime\":1744665088,\"endTime\":1744665094},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"mean to interrupt. \",\"startTime\":1744665094,\"endTime\":1744665098},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Oh, no worries, no worries. You''re you''re a new user with this stuff.\",\"startTime\":1744665098,\"endTime\":1744665102},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"All right, I''m good with that question. Oh, by the way, mine says partner ready \",\"startTime\":1744665102,\"endTime\":1744665107},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"OK.\",\"startTime\":1744665104,\"endTime\":1744665104},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"right now as soon as you hit next. And then when I hit it, if I hit back, for \",\"startTime\":1744665107,\"endTime\":1744665111},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"example, now it''ll tell you waiting like I wanted to go back and I have to wait for you to go back to the last card, otherwise we can''t go forward. \",\"startTime\":1744665111,\"endTime\":1744665119},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"OK.\",\"startTime\":1744665123,\"endTime\":1744665123},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"But OK, now we''ll go forward.\",\"startTime\":1744665125,\"endTime\":1744665126},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"So we have got it. Oh, got it. OK, sorry I was reading the questions simultaneously. \",\"startTime\":1744665126,\"endTime\":1744665130},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"No worries, but that gives me a note that we need to edit this as a new lesson because this one does say take turns sharing with your partner. \",\"startTime\":1744665130,\"endTime\":1744665137},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1744665137,\"endTime\":1744665138},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"The other question was confusing ''cause it. The other question was confusing \",\"startTime\":1744665139,\"endTime\":1744665141},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"''cause it. \",\"startTime\":1744665141,\"endTime\":1744665144},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"If it''s giving us both the same prompt, it''s. It was confusing. Like whatever \",\"startTime\":1744665145,\"endTime\":1744665148},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"I''ll put my thoughts down. \",\"startTime\":1744665148,\"endTime\":1744665151},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah. No, no, exactly. I''m with you.\",\"startTime\":1744665153,\"endTime\":1744665156},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Oops, I just came back by accident. I''m so sorry.\",\"startTime\":1744665155,\"endTime\":1744665158},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"We have to go back. Yeah, no, but it does say ask your partner. So instead of \",\"startTime\":1744665159,\"endTime\":1744665162},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"OK, yeah, but.\",\"startTime\":1744665159,\"endTime\":1744665162},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"take turns sharing that either, I''ll change the prompt on that. \",\"startTime\":1744665162,\"endTime\":1744665166},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Your thoughts are your what time?\",\"startTime\":1744665165,\"endTime\":1744665167},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I''ll change the prompt to be like the third card, take turn sharing, or make it an actual listener in question or cards. \",\"startTime\":1744665170,\"endTime\":1744665179},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Yes, yeah, ''cause it''s.\",\"startTime\":1744665175,\"endTime\":1744665177},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"When it says share your thoughts on your partner''s prompt, I''m like why isn''t my partner''s prompt if I''m looking at it but it''s both of our prompts? If we \",\"startTime\":1744665180,\"endTime\":1744665186},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"both are seeing the same prompt, making the distinction there doesn''t quite make sense. \",\"startTime\":1744665186,\"endTime\":1744665191},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Good feedback.\",\"startTime\":1744665191,\"endTime\":1744665192},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"All right, what are some pros and cons?\",\"startTime\":1744665196,\"endTime\":1744665198},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"What is the?\",\"startTime\":1744665197,\"endTime\":1744665198},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Of using AI in education.\",\"startTime\":1744665201,\"endTime\":1744665203},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Uh, this? I have no idea because I''ve never tried to do it, obviously.\",\"startTime\":1744665205,\"endTime\":1744665212},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Well, you do know because you''re a learner, A lifelong learner, and education is supposed to be about helping learners get better at learning. So if you think \",\"startTime\":1744665211,\"endTime\":1744665218},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"about AI now, today, what are some pros and cons if you''re thinking about even what you know about yourself as a learner or what you would hope others would do? \",\"startTime\":1744665218,\"endTime\":1744665230},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Mm-hmm. I think the pros are what exactly what you and I talked about. I think \",\"startTime\":1744665230,\"endTime\":1744665234},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"AI can be a dialectical partner that can have conversations with you and some people learn a lot better that way versus just reading. It''s a more dynamic \",\"startTime\":1744665234,\"endTime\":1744665243},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"learning experience. Possibly Cons would be when it''s tempting to use AI as \",\"startTime\":1744665243,\"endTime\":1744665247},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"a shortcut instead of an expansive tool, It''s like just like making it do the work for you and not learning anything but just skipping through like. \",\"startTime\":1744665247,\"endTime\":1744665256},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"And cons would also at this point be accuracy issues. It''s like great to dialogue \",\"startTime\":1744665256,\"endTime\":1744665260},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"with an AI but if it just starts hallucinating information at you and you''re learning weird and wrong things, that''s not so good. \",\"startTime\":1744665260,\"endTime\":1744665268},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1744665269,\"endTime\":1744665269},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1744665269,\"endTime\":1744665270},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I''m totally with you pros about going faster, assimilating knowledge, having so much at your fingertips. I think it helps really focus on some things if \",\"startTime\":1744665272,\"endTime\":1744665280},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"we allow it to. Like you were just talking about having the AI tool help you \",\"startTime\":1744665280,\"endTime\":1744665285},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"to create structure and what a wonderful place to know that you can just play and. \",\"startTime\":1744665285,\"endTime\":1744665293},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Mm-hmm.\",\"startTime\":1744665297,\"endTime\":1744665297},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"As you were talking about, you can just engage in rich conversation even with yourself, and then you could take that rich conversation without being mindfully trying to fill in all the details about structure. But then you can have AI \",\"startTime\":1744665298,\"endTime\":1744665310},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"get that structure for you. \",\"startTime\":1744665310,\"endTime\":1744665313},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Kids writing papers, helping encourage them on all those things. There''s so \",\"startTime\":1744665315,\"endTime\":1744665318},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"many pros I can see. And then the cons. \",\"startTime\":1744665318,\"endTime\":1744665321},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I''m with you on that for inaccuracies, but I''m also seeing things like this one was really bothersome to me, Erica reported back from a group. \",\"startTime\":1744665322,\"endTime\":1744665329},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Women in AI.\",\"startTime\":1744665329,\"endTime\":1744665331},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"They''re finding that if even the AI tool thinks that you''re female.\",\"startTime\":1744665333,\"endTime\":1744665338},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Thinks that you''re a girl, You don''t even know for sure that you''re a girl, that the responses, like with tech, are less sophisticated, even thinks you''re a girl. That is the bias, that gender bias that''s built into it. \",\"startTime\":1744665339,\"endTime\":1744665351},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Hmm, interesting.\",\"startTime\":1744665349,\"endTime\":1744665354},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"The bias is there. That''s really problematic. And then for me, I''ve seen some \",\"startTime\":1744665353,\"endTime\":1744665357},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"That''s the thing.\",\"startTime\":1744665356,\"endTime\":1744665358},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"other cons around bias, not like a gender bias, but a a reflection of who we are. The AI tools are just reflecting what we popularly believe or hold true \",\"startTime\":1744665357,\"endTime\":1744665365},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"or what''s out there. \",\"startTime\":1744665365,\"endTime\":1744665369},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And that that''s a, that''s a con. It shouldn''t just reflect it in an example \",\"startTime\":1744665371,\"endTime\":1744665375},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"for me in that regard was I was trying to get an AI tool to. \",\"startTime\":1744665375,\"endTime\":1744665380},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Do an adaptation of a lesson not too long ago. A really quality lesson and the \",\"startTime\":1744665380,\"endTime\":1744665383},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"AI. \",\"startTime\":1744665383,\"endTime\":1744665386},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Said to preload and pre teach, which was totally against the principles and the guidelines and the teaching of the whole of the curriculum. And the lesson \",\"startTime\":1744665388,\"endTime\":1744665396},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1744665391,\"endTime\":1744665391},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"is is a wonderful lesson already about inviting kids in and and activating their previous knowledge, but welcoming them in at welcome welcome mean them in as a learner and the the AI tool totally took what was common out there. Oh, you \",\"startTime\":1744665396,\"endTime\":1744665410},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"got to tell them what to do and do it this way and you''re like. \",\"startTime\":1744665410,\"endTime\":1744665414},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"No, please no. And so I think there''s those cons is that we as educators and \",\"startTime\":1744665415,\"endTime\":1744665419},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"as students both are getting this output from the AI tools and we generally take it at face value is that it''s right because it''s authoritative and it sounds right or it looks good. And I think that''s really damaging if we''re not really \",\"startTime\":1744665419,\"endTime\":1744665431},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"careful consumers, critical consumers with that. \",\"startTime\":1744665431,\"endTime\":1744665435},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah, yeah. That''s a really good point.\",\"startTime\":1744665436,\"endTime\":1744665438},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Now, OK, I''m going to press more and.\",\"startTime\":1744665440,\"endTime\":1744665443},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"We hit.\",\"startTime\":1744665445,\"endTime\":1744665446},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And we did identity and agency, we talked about using it for us.\",\"startTime\":1744665448,\"endTime\":1744665453},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"So we can we get it? I didn''t even think about privacy, to be honest.\",\"startTime\":1744665450,\"endTime\":1744665455},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Hmm, alright. Well, maybe we''ll have to think more on that, OK.\",\"startTime\":1744665457,\"endTime\":1744665461},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Scenario problem solved together. How would you best respond to this situation? \",\"startTime\":1744665468,\"endTime\":1744665473},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Uh, uh.\",\"startTime\":1744665470,\"endTime\":1744665470},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"I''m like, I would just say we''re not going to do that. Thank you. Bye.\",\"startTime\":1744665473,\"endTime\":1744665477},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"I just don''t like, I just don''t think it''s healthy for students. I don''t think \",\"startTime\":1744665479,\"endTime\":1744665483},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"it''s healthy for young people to feel monitored at risk of punishment like. \",\"startTime\":1744665483,\"endTime\":1744665488},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"That''s not the right way to support a growing mind. Like that''s just such bad, \",\"startTime\":1744665489,\"endTime\":1744665493},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"a bad value system to instill in them that like you should do the right thing because you''re being watched and not because. \",\"startTime\":1744665493,\"endTime\":1744665500},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"I''m going to show you the benefit of the positive benefit to your life, of developing a value system that you live, that you embody like I want. \",\"startTime\":1744665500,\"endTime\":1744665509},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Students to pay attention because learning is joyful for them and they see the benefits that learning brings to their lives. Like that''s what I want to encourage \",\"startTime\":1744665510,\"endTime\":1744665518},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"and students or would want to encourage in students, I don''t want students. \",\"startTime\":1744665518,\"endTime\":1744665522},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"To feel like they have to pay attention and they''ll be punished. That''s such \",\"startTime\":1744665523,\"endTime\":1744665526},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"a terrible value system. Terrible, terrible. There''s so many reasons. I would \",\"startTime\":1744665526,\"endTime\":1744665528},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"just be like, we''re not doing that. \",\"startTime\":1744665528,\"endTime\":1744665531},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I think my question to surface that would be right away is how is this going to monitor and what feedback will it give kids? Like tell me more, tell me more \",\"startTime\":1744665532,\"endTime\":1744665542},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1744665540,\"endTime\":1744665541},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"about how this works because if the feedback is. \",\"startTime\":1744665542,\"endTime\":1744665546},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Pass. Your eyes aren''t on the screen and that''s what it''s saying. Or you''re \",\"startTime\":1744665546,\"endTime\":1744665550},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"getting marks for not paying attention that way or. \",\"startTime\":1744665550,\"endTime\":1744665554},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"It''s a negative. We caught you because you weren''t engaging that way versus \",\"startTime\":1744665555,\"endTime\":1744665557},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1744665555,\"endTime\":1744665556},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"the. \",\"startTime\":1744665557,\"endTime\":1744665560},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Flip flop where it was maybe afterwards, and it gave a summary of oh, Cass, here''s a summary of the cool things that you were saying. We noticed XY and \",\"startTime\":1744665560,\"endTime\":1744665567},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Z and. \",\"startTime\":1744665567,\"endTime\":1744665570},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Like I don''t know what they''re talking about for this AI tool that monitors student engagement like. \",\"startTime\":1744665570,\"endTime\":1744665575},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Yeah, it''s it''s a good point that I immediately assumed it would be punitive though. When you''re like, how are they going to monitor? And I was like, Oh \",\"startTime\":1744665574,\"endTime\":1744665582},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"yeah, what if it''s like noticing things and asking questions and like helping guide the student? What if it''s like we noticed your eyes are on the screen. \",\"startTime\":1744665582,\"endTime\":1744665589},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Is everything OK? And, and me personally, when I''m listening, I fidget and, \",\"startTime\":1744665589,\"endTime\":1744665593},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"and like, I''m so aware of this, but like when I''m really listening to someone, I like have to fidget with something and like, I''m like, I look away and I''m like listening and fidgeting. Like that''s my listening mode. But sometimes it. \",\"startTime\":1744665593,\"endTime\":1744665604},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"People is I''m not paying attention.\",\"startTime\":1744665604,\"endTime\":1744665606},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Hey, hey, I have a meeting out here. Sorry.\",\"startTime\":1744665607,\"endTime\":1744665611},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Same. No worries.\",\"startTime\":1744665612,\"endTime\":1744665614},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Umm, I uh, uh, it sometimes reads to people as me not paying attention, but I''m actually deep paying attention. That''s what it''s a signal of and if some \",\"startTime\":1744665613,\"endTime\":1744665619},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"It''s funny that you''re that way.\",\"startTime\":1744665614,\"endTime\":1744665616},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"monitoring tool was like. \",\"startTime\":1744665619,\"endTime\":1744665622},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Just helping, you know, just being like, hey, we''re noticing this or can we do this? Or what if we do it this way? Like it could be really positive assistant. \",\"startTime\":1744665623,\"endTime\":1744665629},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"I didn''t even think of that. I just assumed it would be punitive. \",\"startTime\":1744665629,\"endTime\":1744665633},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Because the popular culture is, that''s how we use. That''s what monitors student \",\"startTime\":1744665635,\"endTime\":1744665638},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"engagement means, yeah. \",\"startTime\":1744665638,\"endTime\":1744665640},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Yeah, totally.\",\"startTime\":1744665640,\"endTime\":1744665641},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"I''m so sorry. Whoop. I Oh, there you are. I dropped the screen really quick. \",\"startTime\":1744665643,\"endTime\":1744665645},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And.\",\"startTime\":1744665643,\"endTime\":1744665643},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"You''re back. \",\"startTime\":1744665645,\"endTime\":1744665647},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Oh by the way for future ones, because sometimes the words are like a lot on the screen. If you just touch the screen not on the words the they go away. \",\"startTime\":1744665649,\"endTime\":1744665657},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Yeah, I I figured that out. But I just like accidentally like because my screen \",\"startTime\":1744665656,\"endTime\":1744665660},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"is broken. I accidentally like moved the camera, but now you''re back. \",\"startTime\":1744665660,\"endTime\":1744665665},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Oh, got it, got it. It''s all good.\",\"startTime\":1744665666,\"endTime\":1744665668},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Cool.\",\"startTime\":1744665668,\"endTime\":1744665668},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I think also along that way, if the scenario is your school, your school''s considering adopting a new AI tool that monitors student engagement during online classes. \",\"startTime\":1744665668,\"endTime\":1744665678},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I would, I would be asking questions about, OK, so who like what''s the criteria that you''re using to measure engagement? And is this, is this what teachers \",\"startTime\":1744665679,\"endTime\":1744665687},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"are doing and what students are doing? And is it to facilitate and is it in \",\"startTime\":1744665687,\"endTime\":1744665692},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"a positive or is this a deficit minded approach? Like I would want to know and \",\"startTime\":1744665692,\"endTime\":1744665696},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"ask those kind of questions because. \",\"startTime\":1744665696,\"endTime\":1744665701},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1744665702,\"endTime\":1744665703},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Like even engagement. I''m so sorry if you''re doing a monitoring tool that is \",\"startTime\":1744665702,\"endTime\":1744665706},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"measuring student engagement but the teacher is using horrible practices or bad practices just want want want want want for an hour. Don''t put it on the \",\"startTime\":1744665706,\"endTime\":1744665715},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1744665714,\"endTime\":1744665715},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"kid monitoring student has to start. That''s why I''m like wasn''t going. What''s \",\"startTime\":1744665715,\"endTime\":1744665719},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1744665719,\"endTime\":1744665721},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"the criteria? \",\"startTime\":1744665719,\"endTime\":1744665723},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"It''s like is this?\",\"startTime\":1744665722,\"endTime\":1744665723},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Gateway one is the teacher doing.\",\"startTime\":1744665724,\"endTime\":1744665727},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"I''m like, is the student engaged? Sorry, go on.\",\"startTime\":1744665725,\"endTime\":1744665728},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Yeah, no, I want to call it out. It doesn''t say gateway one for the monitoring \",\"startTime\":1744665728,\"endTime\":1744665731},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"tool. Is the teacher using effective teaching strategies, yes or no? If no, \",\"startTime\":1744665731,\"endTime\":1744665735},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"then don''t worry. \",\"startTime\":1744665735,\"endTime\":1744665738},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1744665736,\"endTime\":1744665738},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"It''s a really good, really good perspective. Really, really holistic, like whole \",\"startTime\":1744665740,\"endTime\":1744665743},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"picture thinking. It''s really good. \",\"startTime\":1744665743,\"endTime\":1744665747},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I love it.\",\"startTime\":1744665747,\"endTime\":1744665748},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"All right, Hard ready.\",\"startTime\":1744665749,\"endTime\":1744665751},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Alright, umm.\",\"startTime\":1744665752,\"endTime\":1744665753},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"I know what I''ve taken from this conversation. I thought just that question \",\"startTime\":1744665753,\"endTime\":1744665756},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"we just had, I thought the way you were like. \",\"startTime\":1744665756,\"endTime\":1744665759},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"You responded by asking questions 1st and not leaving the judgment. I was like, \",\"startTime\":1744665760,\"endTime\":1744665763},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"that was a powerful learning moment for me to be like, like it was a really nice reminder like always ask questions and always think about the whole thing. \",\"startTime\":1744665763,\"endTime\":1744665769},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"And also this idea that. \",\"startTime\":1744665769,\"endTime\":1744665772},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"A tool like that is only capturing partial information. It''s like, OK, kids \",\"startTime\":1744665773,\"endTime\":1744665776},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"are struggling to pay attention. It might not just be the kid. Like, what are \",\"startTime\":1744665776,\"endTime\":1744665778},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"the other factors that we should be considering? I thought that was really powerful, \",\"startTime\":1744665778,\"endTime\":1744665781},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"and I feel like I learned from that. \",\"startTime\":1744665781,\"endTime\":1744665783},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Oh, I love it. I love it.\",\"startTime\":1744665785,\"endTime\":1744665786},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"Thank you for the great conversation. And it was something right away early \",\"startTime\":1744665787,\"endTime\":1744665790},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"on in the conversation that I''m going to take away and try. \",\"startTime\":1744665790,\"endTime\":1744665794},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"And you said that after you were doing your thing, you were going to just go for a walk. And and I was like, I don''t remember exactly what you said, but \",\"startTime\":1744665794,\"endTime\":1744665802},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Oh yeah.\",\"startTime\":1744665801,\"endTime\":1744665802},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"taking that time to go for a walk, then meditate and think deeply about stuff like. \",\"startTime\":1744665802,\"endTime\":1744665809},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I need to do that more in my practice, so I like to do it. I know I should do \",\"startTime\":1744665811,\"endTime\":1744665815},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"that. I have done that at times, but right now as I''m building routines again. \",\"startTime\":1744665815,\"endTime\":1744665819},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"I want to put that into practice and not just go from one thing to the next thing to the next thing, but be really mindful so. \",\"startTime\":1744665820,\"endTime\":1744665826},{\"speaker\":\"11978\",\"text\":\"Critical. OK, I''m going to hit end now.\",\"startTime\":1744665826,\"endTime\":1744665829},{\"speaker\":\"8084\",\"text\":\"All right. Well, Bonita.\",\"startTime\":1744665828,\"endTime\":1744665830}]"', '2025-04-30 20:57:08.979721+00', '2025-04-30 20:57:08.979721+00', '{"type": "PAIR", "duration": 1383, "created_at": "2025-04-30T20:57:08.931Z", "session_title": "Exploring the Relationship between Learning, Identity, and AI", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "1700", "name": "Exploring the Relationship between Learning, Identity, and AI", "tags": [{"name": "draft-leaders"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('c2ec1559-c6c2-4dac-8c29-118e4e55e932', '6591e553-8215-4832-843f-a15c716b5863', '137782', '"[{\"speaker\":\"11955\",\"text\":\"What are you? What are you getting better at? I''m going to mute over again. \",\"startTime\":1742589433,\"endTime\":1742589437},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"Hey, Mike.\",\"startTime\":1742589435,\"endTime\":1742589436},{\"speaker\":\"11955\",\"text\":\"What are you getting better at besides AI fluency? \",\"startTime\":1742589437,\"endTime\":1742589440},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"Bike skills, it''s the like the realize I put a lot of emphasis on endurance that was great, but now I got to mess around with being able to really dynamically move and not fall off bike. And so that building the body stuff that can do \",\"startTime\":1742589444,\"endTime\":1742589456},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"it without me thinking about it to like. \",\"startTime\":1742589456,\"endTime\":1742589460},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"All the parts being on a bike like that.\",\"startTime\":1742589461,\"endTime\":1742589463},{\"speaker\":\"11955\",\"text\":\"Very cool. Like, uh.\",\"startTime\":1742589464,\"endTime\":1742589466},{\"speaker\":\"11955\",\"text\":\"Body bike dynamics The athletics of of getting the bike to go where you want to go, when you want to go there. \",\"startTime\":1742589468,\"endTime\":1742589473},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah, like in swimming, I can like I can get hit by crazy waves. I can, \",\"startTime\":1742589474,\"endTime\":1742589480},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"I can like navigate swimming as if I am a part of water. \",\"startTime\":1742589480,\"endTime\":1742589483},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"And it''s wild. It''s like if you watch me in water and Dale on a bike, like that \",\"startTime\":1742589483,\"endTime\":1742589486},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"bike is a part of Dale''s body. Like he''s just, it''s a part. And that when you \",\"startTime\":1742589486,\"endTime\":1742589488},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"watch me on a bike, you''re like, oh. \",\"startTime\":1742589488,\"endTime\":1742589491},{\"speaker\":\"11955\",\"text\":\"Yeah, when Dale and I share like ripping around our little towns on our tiny BMX bikes with our friends, jumping off of things. \",\"startTime\":1742589493,\"endTime\":1742589499},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"And.\",\"startTime\":1742589494,\"endTime\":1742589494},{\"speaker\":\"11955\",\"text\":\"I''m sure it''s like.\",\"startTime\":1742589499,\"endTime\":1742589500},{\"speaker\":\"11955\",\"text\":\"10,000 hours, it''s just so much time with your friends saying like, I bet you can''t and you''d be like, let me try. So it''s a lot, it''s a lot of bike time. \",\"startTime\":1742589500,\"endTime\":1742589509},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"Yes.\",\"startTime\":1742589504,\"endTime\":1742589505},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"Yeah. And that like I was in a pool, you know, I think I got up to like 20 in \",\"startTime\":1742589509,\"endTime\":1742589513},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"a row spinning around underwater. Like I could do like 5 lengths of my pool \",\"startTime\":1742589513,\"endTime\":1742589516},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"underwater. I could do pool basketball. Like I, I just so much pool like water \",\"startTime\":1742589516,\"endTime\":1742589520},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"related things that my body and water does. \",\"startTime\":1742589520,\"endTime\":1742589523},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"Or I''m like, yeah, I could do that.\",\"startTime\":1742589524,\"endTime\":1742589526},{\"speaker\":\"11955\",\"text\":\"Yeah, cool.\",\"startTime\":1742589527,\"endTime\":1742589528},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"Yeah, Yep.\",\"startTime\":1742589527,\"endTime\":1742589528},{\"speaker\":\"11955\",\"text\":\"It''ll transfer.\",\"startTime\":1742589528,\"endTime\":1742589530},{\"speaker\":\"11955\",\"text\":\"Listen to a podcast. The latest Joe Rogan podcast is with Josh Waitzkin, who \",\"startTime\":1742589531,\"endTime\":1742589535},{\"speaker\":\"11955\",\"text\":\"is one of my favorite thinkers in the world. And so it''s funny hearing. \",\"startTime\":1742589535,\"endTime\":1742589540},{\"speaker\":\"11955\",\"text\":\"Joe be a kind of dummy, but like has a platform and Josh being like the smartest. \",\"startTime\":1742589541,\"endTime\":1742589546},{\"speaker\":\"11955\",\"text\":\"Speak like Thinker that I''ve run across and having them try to have a conversation is very silly. But they talk about bikes for a little while and they''re in a \",\"startTime\":1742589546,\"endTime\":1742589552},{\"speaker\":\"11955\",\"text\":\"very, very frustrating way. \",\"startTime\":1742589552,\"endTime\":1742589555},{\"speaker\":\"11955\",\"text\":\"So enjoy not listening to that.\",\"startTime\":1742589557,\"endTime\":1742589559},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"Sounds good, but that is fun to hear people playing that. OK. Hey Mike, how \",\"startTime\":1742589559,\"endTime\":1742589564},{\"speaker\":\"11955\",\"text\":\"All right, moving forward.\",\"startTime\":1742589562,\"endTime\":1742589564},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"has AI changed your work as an educator or leader of educators so far? \",\"startTime\":1742589564,\"endTime\":1742589569},{\"speaker\":\"11955\",\"text\":\"Nothing. I''m not really using it. I think that AI is a little spooky.\",\"startTime\":1742589573,\"endTime\":1742589578},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"Do you mind if I ask what Spooks you the most?\",\"startTime\":1742589580,\"endTime\":1742589586},{\"speaker\":\"11955\",\"text\":\"I mean, you''ve seen Terminator, right?\",\"startTime\":1742589585,\"endTime\":1742589587},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"More recently than not, yes I did finally see Terminator. But doesn''t he get \",\"startTime\":1742589589,\"endTime\":1742589592},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"like nice ''cause we I watched a bunch of them in a row. \",\"startTime\":1742589592,\"endTime\":1742589596},{\"speaker\":\"11955\",\"text\":\"In character, out of character. I don''t think I''ve seen it.\",\"startTime\":1742589598,\"endTime\":1742589601},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"I feel like because at first he''s like, it''s like, oh, but then it''s like he''s nice or something. \",\"startTime\":1742589602,\"endTime\":1742589605},{\"speaker\":\"11955\",\"text\":\"Yeah, I guess to be a more authentic I, I was with hands last night at hands, he said. I don''t think we''re gonna get smarter. I think we''re gonna, we''re gonna \",\"startTime\":1742589607,\"endTime\":1742589612},{\"speaker\":\"11955\",\"text\":\"get, we''re gonna get. \",\"startTime\":1742589612,\"endTime\":1742589614},{\"speaker\":\"11955\",\"text\":\"Complacent and lazy.\",\"startTime\":1742589616,\"endTime\":1742589618},{\"speaker\":\"11955\",\"text\":\"That might be another.\",\"startTime\":1742589620,\"endTime\":1742589621},{\"speaker\":\"11955\",\"text\":\"Worst case.\",\"startTime\":1742589622,\"endTime\":1742589623},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"Yeah, I did have my first experience where I think someone was trying to push me to a voice agent. \",\"startTime\":1742589624,\"endTime\":1742589629},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"And so she was probably, it was good. I was like, sure, she saw me on a slack. \",\"startTime\":1742589629,\"endTime\":1742589634},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"Engage with me like I think she would. You. You''re the leading edge people. \",\"startTime\":1742589635,\"endTime\":1742589637},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"Engage with your people. \",\"startTime\":1742589637,\"endTime\":1742589640},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"I was like, let''s ride this trampoline. Then she was like, don''t you want to \",\"startTime\":1742589640,\"endTime\":1742589643},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"meet up? And I was like, hey, I''m already on your calendar. And then it''s like, \",\"startTime\":1742589643,\"endTime\":1742589645},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"oh, sorry. And so I''m like, then the calendar invite came from a very weird \",\"startTime\":1742589645,\"endTime\":1742589648},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"e-mail. \",\"startTime\":1742589648,\"endTime\":1742589651},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"Then she missed it and so I''m sitting on there and then two minutes and it''s, hey, I got to jump in my car. Would you be up for a call? \",\"startTime\":1742589652,\"endTime\":1742589658},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"And I was like this, it just didn''t feel authentic. I was so I''m fascinated. \",\"startTime\":1742589659,\"endTime\":1742589663},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"I''m like, oh, would I have been on with her truly in her car? Would I have been \",\"startTime\":1742589663,\"endTime\":1742589667},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"on with someone pretending to be her on the phone? Would I be in on with a voice \",\"startTime\":1742589667,\"endTime\":1742589671},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"agent? And I kind of wanted to be like, hey, could I just like get on with your \",\"startTime\":1742589671,\"endTime\":1742589674},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"voice agent because this is super interesting. Even though I''m deeply annoyed \",\"startTime\":1742589674,\"endTime\":1742589678},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"that you''re a liar, like, and but that kind of thing of like. \",\"startTime\":1742589678,\"endTime\":1742589682},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"The feeling hadness of it, I was excited as an AI learner and I was really annoyed as like a human person who I take these calls because we we like genuinely are trying to connect about. \",\"startTime\":1742589685,\"endTime\":1742589695},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"Educationy things or?\",\"startTime\":1742589695,\"endTime\":1742589697},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"Could help each other in the world.\",\"startTime\":1742589697,\"endTime\":1742589698},{\"speaker\":\"11955\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah. So like that be being manipulated very well, will, is not what we \",\"startTime\":1742589698,\"endTime\":1742589703},{\"speaker\":\"11955\",\"text\":\"want. But like we actually do want teachers to manipulate students to learn \",\"startTime\":1742589703,\"endTime\":1742589707},{\"speaker\":\"11955\",\"text\":\"important shit. Like that''s kind of our job. \",\"startTime\":1742589707,\"endTime\":1742589711},{\"speaker\":\"11955\",\"text\":\"Yeah, it''s it''s to manipulate in a direction.\",\"startTime\":1742589713,\"endTime\":1742589715},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1742589713,\"endTime\":1742589714},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"Yes, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1742589715,\"endTime\":1742589716},{\"speaker\":\"11955\",\"text\":\"Yeah, so let''s put it in front of teachers and not just advertisers.\",\"startTime\":1742589718,\"endTime\":1742589721},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"Yes, yes.\",\"startTime\":1742589722,\"endTime\":1742589724},{\"speaker\":\"11955\",\"text\":\"Yeah, let''s let''s click through a little bit because like this is kind of working and it''s hard. Of course, I''d love to have this conversation with you. \",\"startTime\":1742589723,\"endTime\":1742589729},{\"speaker\":\"11954\",\"text\":\"Yep, agreed. Agreed. You love it, love it.\",\"startTime\":1742589728,\"endTime\":1742589732}]"', '2025-04-30 20:57:09.450309+00', '2025-04-30 20:57:09.450309+00', '{"type": "PAIR", "duration": 304, "created_at": "2025-04-30T20:57:09.424Z", "session_title": "#ai_learning_tools", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "190", "name": "#ai_learning_tools", "tags": [{"name": "Dream Camp"}, {"name": "AI in Education"}, {"name": "Freemium"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('fd77b282-2177-42b0-8588-c1fc0b7386de', '0df8e918-c6f4-4615-aadf-42c257edb6f4', '137148', '"[{\"speaker\":\"11887\",\"text\":\"My name''s Kelly Spahn. I teach school math in Federal Way. I''m also an educational \",\"startTime\":1739914931,\"endTime\":1739914935},{\"speaker\":\"11887\",\"text\":\"consultant for AI. \",\"startTime\":1739914935,\"endTime\":1739914938},{\"speaker\":\"11887\",\"text\":\"And I really just hope to connect with people that are in AI and education and learn different use cases and just become the best educator I can be. \",\"startTime\":1739914938,\"endTime\":1739914949},{\"speaker\":\"11887\",\"text\":\"Dance for teaching and learning is very much learned by doing and being involved in an active participant. The person doing is the person learning. I am also \",\"startTime\":1739914994,\"endTime\":1739915004},{\"speaker\":\"11887\",\"text\":\"got into teaching for the idea of liberation and freedom. So knowing that the \",\"startTime\":1739915004,\"endTime\":1739915009},{\"speaker\":\"11887\",\"text\":\"more knowledge you have. \",\"startTime\":1739915009,\"endTime\":1739915013},{\"speaker\":\"11887\",\"text\":\"The more power you have and justice knowledge to navigate the world and the systems that affect you. \",\"startTime\":1739915013,\"endTime\":1739915020},{\"speaker\":\"11887\",\"text\":\"My primary flow activity is anything creative, so I love to create digital colleges using the Pinterest tool. I dabble in writing poetry and also cooking is one \",\"startTime\":1739915052,\"endTime\":1739915060},{\"speaker\":\"11887\",\"text\":\"of my favorites. \",\"startTime\":1739915060,\"endTime\":1739915064}]"', '2025-04-30 20:57:09.392276+00', '2025-04-30 20:57:09.392276+00', '{"type": "SINGLE", "duration": 70, "created_at": "2025-04-30T20:57:09.348Z", "session_title": "Welcome to sideby!", "knowledgeNodes": [{"id": "22", "name": "Welcome to sideby!", "tags": [{"name": "Active"}, {"name": "ColumbiaSelkirk"}, {"name": "Leaders of Color"}]}], "manually_stored": true}'),
	('b7a85374-2963-4e30-b03a-542e077f727c', '59e9f386-0ecc-4201-99dd-802f7f8e7b33', '138260', '"[{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"Who is this person?\",\"startTime\":1745506809,\"endTime\":1745506810},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"Hey, how are you?\",\"startTime\":1745506811,\"endTime\":1745506813},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Hi friend.\",\"startTime\":1745506813,\"endTime\":1745506813},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"I''m all right, Yeah. What time is it for you?\",\"startTime\":1745506813,\"endTime\":1745506816},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"It is.\",\"startTime\":1745506817,\"endTime\":1745506818},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"8:00 in the morning. 8:00 AM.\",\"startTime\":1745506818,\"endTime\":1745506820},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"That''s not the worst.\",\"startTime\":1745506821,\"endTime\":1745506822},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"No, I need what?\",\"startTime\":1745506826,\"endTime\":1745506828},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"Like 4 in the afternoon or something there.\",\"startTime\":1745506830,\"endTime\":1745506832},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Great it is. And it''s sunny. It looks like it''s sunny for you too.\",\"startTime\":1745506832,\"endTime\":1745506838},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"This is our new place. We moved to Tucson. Yeah, it''s.\",\"startTime\":1745506837,\"endTime\":1745506841},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Look at that pool.\",\"startTime\":1745506840,\"endTime\":1745506841},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"You''re in Tucson.\",\"startTime\":1745506843,\"endTime\":1745506844},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"Are boys happy?\",\"startTime\":1745506846,\"endTime\":1745506847},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Whoa. Aww.\",\"startTime\":1745506848,\"endTime\":1745506849},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"Yeah, we moved to Tucson, Anna and I.\",\"startTime\":1745506849,\"endTime\":1745506851},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"And I''m loving it. We''re loving it.\",\"startTime\":1745506851,\"endTime\":1745506853},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"This is this is mine right now.\",\"startTime\":1745506854,\"endTime\":1745506856},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"Oh.\",\"startTime\":1745506859,\"endTime\":1745506860},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"There she is.\",\"startTime\":1745506861,\"endTime\":1745506862},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"Oh, what''s her name?\",\"startTime\":1745506862,\"endTime\":1745506864},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Say hi.\",\"startTime\":1745506863,\"endTime\":1745506864},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Callie.\",\"startTime\":1745506867,\"endTime\":1745506868},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"Callie, oh sweet puppy.\",\"startTime\":1745506868,\"endTime\":1745506870},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"Oh, how are you?\",\"startTime\":1745506870,\"endTime\":1745506872},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Dude, I''m all right. Life is like.\",\"startTime\":1745506873,\"endTime\":1745506876},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Challenging and exciting and there''s like opportunity and I''m trying to figure out. \",\"startTime\":1745506878,\"endTime\":1745506884},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"You know, like some some deep stuff around, like what is it that I''m really doing with my life? \",\"startTime\":1745506886,\"endTime\":1745506892},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"No big deal.\",\"startTime\":1745506895,\"endTime\":1745506896},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"Just nothing much, you know? Gotta figure out a couple things, like where my \",\"startTime\":1745506899,\"endTime\":1745506902},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"socks go and I reorganize them. \",\"startTime\":1745506902,\"endTime\":1745506905},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Exactly. Exactly.\",\"startTime\":1745506905,\"endTime\":1745506906},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"Oh, is this is this because just life in your that place where you''re seeing all of the stuff, or are you getting like impetus from work things or? \",\"startTime\":1745506907,\"endTime\":1745506918},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Yeah, I mean, my job, like my, my coaching gig continues to like be pretty lackluster as far as like, I mean, it pays. It''s like the opposite of what most people \",\"startTime\":1745506920,\"endTime\":1745506930},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"like actually. I have the dream of what most people want. And it''s like my worst \",\"startTime\":1745506930,\"endTime\":1745506935},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"nightmare. Like my work expects nothing of me. Like no teacher wants to be with \",\"startTime\":1745506935,\"endTime\":1745506940},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"me. And my job is like, we''ll just keep paying, don''t leave. \",\"startTime\":1745506940,\"endTime\":1745506945},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"I''m like but I want to actually do work.\",\"startTime\":1745506947,\"endTime\":1745506950},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"I think I wanna actually like make the world a better place. That''s why I''m \",\"startTime\":1745506950,\"endTime\":1745506953},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"here. That''s what I do like, like I wanna. Yeah, yeah, yeah. So I, I like, that''s \",\"startTime\":1745506953,\"endTime\":1745506956},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"Umm, that is so frustrating, Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1745506955,\"endTime\":1745506959},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"why this year I''ve taken on some outside of work stuff. That''s why I''m doing \",\"startTime\":1745506956,\"endTime\":1745506960},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"the BTC conference, which is like, awesome. I love doing that. It''s really good \",\"startTime\":1745506960,\"endTime\":1745506963},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"work. \",\"startTime\":1745506963,\"endTime\":1745506966},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Umm, I''m doing.\",\"startTime\":1745506970,\"endTime\":1745506972},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Roberts Consultants Workshop.\",\"startTime\":1745506972,\"endTime\":1745506974},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Which is really, really cool and teaching me a lot of things about just like what that looks like. \",\"startTime\":1745506976,\"endTime\":1745506980},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"And I''ve been going to some new international conferences and like experiencing that I presented in Switzerland last month. \",\"startTime\":1745506981,\"endTime\":1745506989},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"Awesome.\",\"startTime\":1745506991,\"endTime\":1745506991},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Yeah, that''s fine.\",\"startTime\":1745506992,\"endTime\":1745506994},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Umm and yeah, I just like, I think so there''s like 2 kind of big unknowns down the Pike right now for me just to like really get into it. They''re the kind \",\"startTime\":1745506995,\"endTime\":1745507003},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"of things where like, I don''t know where they''re gonna go. So like it''s, I feel \",\"startTime\":1745507003,\"endTime\":1745507007},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"nervous to like talk about them because. \",\"startTime\":1745507007,\"endTime\":1745507011},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"I like, I don''t know if it''s just gonna like turn into nothing or if it''s gonna turn into something. Do you know what I mean? \",\"startTime\":1745507014,\"endTime\":1745507019},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Umm, but.\",\"startTime\":1745507020,\"endTime\":1745507021},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"One is I''m meeting with Peter in.\",\"startTime\":1745507021,\"endTime\":1745507025},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Prague in a couple weeks.\",\"startTime\":1745507027,\"endTime\":1745507029},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"To talk about joining his European team.\",\"startTime\":1745507030,\"endTime\":1745507033},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"Oh.\",\"startTime\":1745507035,\"endTime\":1745507035},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"So I don''t know what that means. And I don''t like, I don''t want BTC to be my \",\"startTime\":1745507035,\"endTime\":1745507039},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"wife. It''s not like my wife, you know, But it''s also like a really great opportunity. \",\"startTime\":1745507039,\"endTime\":1745507043},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"And Chase is like, why wouldn''t you do this? Like it''s kind of a no brainer, \",\"startTime\":1745507043,\"endTime\":1745507046},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1745507043,\"endTime\":1745507044},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"right? Yeah. And I was like, you don''t have a European team. And Peter was like, \",\"startTime\":1745507046,\"endTime\":1745507050},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"Across Europe, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1745507049,\"endTime\":1745507051},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"that''s correct. \",\"startTime\":1745507050,\"endTime\":1745507054},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Like OK, he has two people in Denmark that just work in Denmark.\",\"startTime\":1745507057,\"endTime\":1745507062},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Right. I''m like, OK.\",\"startTime\":1745507067,\"endTime\":1745507068},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"Oh, I''m hearing so much of like the the space you''re in and I totally know what that''s like being in a district or with a school and you have a position. \",\"startTime\":1745507068,\"endTime\":1745507076},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"And I just started cashing in my sick days. I''m like, it''s fresh snow today. \",\"startTime\":1745507076,\"endTime\":1745507079},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"I can go ski because none of you want me to be in your rooms or in your meetings. \",\"startTime\":1745507079,\"endTime\":1745507082},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"And you don''t want to do any of the stuff that you said you wanted to do. We \",\"startTime\":1745507082,\"endTime\":1745507085},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"built out your plans, but you''re all like. \",\"startTime\":1745507085,\"endTime\":1745507088},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"Or you, you switch plans up at the last minute and you don''t come to the meeting that you said you wanted to do to get these things done or do these and you''re like. \",\"startTime\":1745507090,\"endTime\":1745507099},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1745507094,\"endTime\":1745507096},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"What am I supposed to do? And then I''m also hearing.\",\"startTime\":1745507099,\"endTime\":1745507101},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Yeah, yeah.\",\"startTime\":1745507100,\"endTime\":1745507102},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"Like there''s so many cool opportunities out there. It feels like the the land \",\"startTime\":1745507101,\"endTime\":1745507104},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"of hope where you''re like, oh, I could see that and I could see the Earth is Vista. But then every time you like move forward towards it, you see there''s \",\"startTime\":1745507104,\"endTime\":1745507110},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"this huge Cliff and you have no idea how to get there. You''re like, I don''t \",\"startTime\":1745507110,\"endTime\":1745507113},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"know if I could get there. \",\"startTime\":1745507113,\"endTime\":1745507116},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Yeah, well, the.\",\"startTime\":1745507118,\"endTime\":1745507120},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"And then this BTC thing sounds amazing because it''s great work. You''re well \",\"startTime\":1745507118,\"endTime\":1745507123},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"qualified, you would be amazing at it. It''s a good crew. It pays well. \",\"startTime\":1745507123,\"endTime\":1745507128},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Thank you.\",\"startTime\":1745507126,\"endTime\":1745507127},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"But it''s not your. Why? So how do you use that? If you use it to help get you \",\"startTime\":1745507128,\"endTime\":1745507131},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"or grow the way you want to grow? \",\"startTime\":1745507131,\"endTime\":1745507135},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Right, right. How do I use it as leverage? And like, I think what I figured \",\"startTime\":1745507135,\"endTime\":1745507139},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"out is like what I want to do right, ''cause like Graham was here, Graham Fletcher was here in February and kept just being like, Noble, what''s your North Star? \",\"startTime\":1745507139,\"endTime\":1745507146},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"CS GO.\",\"startTime\":1745507145,\"endTime\":1745507145},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Like where like what is it that''s driving you? Where are you going? And I was \",\"startTime\":1745507146,\"endTime\":1745507150},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"like, honestly, I just love working with other coaches. Like I want to support \",\"startTime\":1745507150,\"endTime\":1745507154},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"other coaches that are like in a similar position where like this is where I always feel like I''m at my best is when I''m able to support other coaches and like that''s not really a thing that''s out there very much right now. It''s like. \",\"startTime\":1745507154,\"endTime\":1745507165},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"How do I develop myself as like the coaches coach specializing in like elementary school math coaches? Like that''s the niche right there. And it''s something that \",\"startTime\":1745507166,\"endTime\":1745507174},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"I do feel really passionate about, but then like I also feel really passionate about like parent education and like. \",\"startTime\":1745507174,\"endTime\":1745507183},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"You know, like working with students, like all these other things, right? So \",\"startTime\":1745507184,\"endTime\":1745507188},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"I''m like, is that gonna pigeonhole me into a place where, like, anyway, so it''s just a lot of questions. It''s all exciting. It''s all really good stuff. And \",\"startTime\":1745507188,\"endTime\":1745507195},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"I also have to say, my kids currently get free tuition at my school. \",\"startTime\":1745507195,\"endTime\":1745507199},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"So I can''t leave my job.\",\"startTime\":1745507201,\"endTime\":1745507203},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"Y viaje.\",\"startTime\":1745507204,\"endTime\":1745507205},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"I would just encourage you to relish the spaces that you have there.\",\"startTime\":1745507208,\"endTime\":1745507211},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"They know that it''s not perfect, but they know that you being there is better than you not being there. If they have the money and funds, then go for it. \",\"startTime\":1745507211,\"endTime\":1745507218},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Yeah, Yeah, Exactly. Exactly. Yeah.\",\"startTime\":1745507216,\"endTime\":1745507219},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"Yeah, you''ll figure it out. It''s gonna be a fun adventure.\",\"startTime\":1745507220,\"endTime\":1745507222},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Yeah, it sure is. So tell me what''s going on.\",\"startTime\":1745507223,\"endTime\":1745507225},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"You got this one.\",\"startTime\":1745507224,\"endTime\":1745507225},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"So you made a huge move.\",\"startTime\":1745507225,\"endTime\":1745507227},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"Yeah, I left the the education service district because I felt in very much what you were saying is there''s all of these things that we could do, all of these banners of equity and goals and purpose statements and vision things and. \",\"startTime\":1745507229,\"endTime\":1745507243},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"And yet we we weren''t really getting anything done. And it was overly frustrating. \",\"startTime\":1745507244,\"endTime\":1745507248},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"And then also, I had planned out like, OK, I was thinking last spring would be a great time for me. It would have been the end of 4 1/2 years. I think it \",\"startTime\":1745507248,\"endTime\":1745507256},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"was at my position about then to do a lump. She''s like, OK, what are you gonna \",\"startTime\":1745507256,\"endTime\":1745507260},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"do, Jeff? And. \",\"startTime\":1745507260,\"endTime\":1745507263},{\"speaker\":\"12002\",\"text\":\"Uh, OK.\",\"startTime\":1745507262,\"endTime\":1745507263},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"Moving, uh.\",\"startTime\":1745507265,\"endTime\":1745507266},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"Out of that space and then in with Erica and Mike to focus on, OK, what are we gonna do next? And we spent last summer and fall. \",\"startTime\":1745507266,\"endTime\":1745507274},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"Going through systematically, what is it that we could do? OK, now what what \",\"startTime\":1745507275,\"endTime\":1745507278},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"is it that we''re going to do and what''s the data and feedback that we got? And \",\"startTime\":1745507278,\"endTime\":1745507282},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"then by the end of November closing out that six month cycle of OK, what did we really do and what are we going to do next? The team decision was let''s do \",\"startTime\":1745507282,\"endTime\":1745507290},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"side by and when Erica showed me. \",\"startTime\":1745507290,\"endTime\":1745507293},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"It was great too ''cause it wasn''t AI generated. She just wrote it for each of \",\"startTime\":1745507294,\"endTime\":1745507296},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"the three of us. Little blurbs about us. \",\"startTime\":1745507296,\"endTime\":1745507299},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",\"text\":\"And when she put that up and she shared it with us members on a Friday.\",\"startTime\":1745507300,\"endTime\":1745507304},{\"speaker\":\"12004\",